'''Oliver James <!-- DO NOT ADD OLLIE AS A NICKNAME PER MOS:NICKNAME-->Bearman''' ({{IPAc-en|b|ɛər|m|ə|n}}; born 8 May 2005) is a British [[racing driver]] who competes in [[Formula One]] for [[Haas F1 Team|Haas]].

Born and raised in [[Chelmsford]], Bearman began competitive [[kart racing]] aged seven, winning several national and continental titles. Graduating to [[junior formulae]] in 2020, Bearman won his first title at the [[2021 Italian F4 Championship]], also winning the [[2021 ADAC Formula 4 Championship|ADAC F4 Championship]] that year, both with [[Van Amersfoort]]. He then competed in [[FIA Formula 3]] in {{FIAF3|2022}}, finishing third in his rookie season with [[Prema Racing|Prema]]. Bearman progressed to [[FIA Formula 2]] in {{F2|2023}}, finishing sixth that year and winning several races across two seasons.

A member of the [[Ferrari Driver Academy]] since 2022, Bearman was a reserve driver for both [[Scuderia Ferrari|Ferrari]] and [[Haas F1 Team|Haas]] in {{F1|2024}}, substituting for [[Carlos Sainz Jr.]] in [[2024 Saudi Arabian Grand Prix|Saudi Arabia]]—making his Formula One debut at the age of eighteen—and for [[Kevin Magnussen]] in [[2024 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|Azerbaijan]] and [[2024 São Paulo Grand Prix|São Paulo]], becoming the youngest-ever driver to compete for Ferrari at the former. Bearman joined Haas as a full-time driver in {{F1|2025}} alongside [[Esteban Ocon]]. Bearman is contracted to remain at Haas until at least the end of the 2027 season.

== Early and personal life ==
Oliver James Bearman was born on 8 May 2005 to David and Terri Bearman in [[London Borough of Havering|Havering]], London.<ref name=Silverman>{{cite news|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2024/03/10/oliver-bearman-f1-ferrari-grand-prix-estelle-ogilvy/|work=The Telegraph|title=How Oliver Bearman went from Chelmsford to Formula One in record time |date=10 March 2024|last=Silverman|first=Rosa}}{{subscription required}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/6wK9o5XmTgYSaLKDPi5ACS/in-profile-oliver-bearman|title=In profile: Oliver Bearman|date=9 August 2022|publisher=FIA Formula 3 Championship}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.thetimes.com/article/oliver-bearman-f1-interview-18-year-old-ferrari-x7xvcjw3p|work=[[The Times]]|title=Oliver Bearman: No lunch, hug from Lewis and a bad back – my F1 debut|date=15 March 2024|last=Westerby|first=John}}{{subscription required}}</ref>{{Dubious|Place of birth: Chelmsford or Havering?|date=June 2026}} He has a younger brother, [[Thomas Bearman]] (who is also a racing driver), and a sister. His father is the founder and chief executive officer of the insurance firm Aventum Group.<ref name=Silverman/> Bearman grew up in [[Chelmsford]], Essex, where he attended [[King Edward VI Grammar School, Chelmsford|King Edward VI Grammar School]]. Bearman left school at the age of sixteen to join the [[Ferrari Driver Academy]] in [[Modena]], Italy.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/f1-oliver-bearman-ferrari-saudi-arabia-b2509373.html|work=The Independent|title=Who is Ollie Bearman? Essex boy with Italian twang driving for Ferrari at Saudi Arabian Grand Prix|date=10 March 2024|last=Duncan|first=Philip}}</ref>

Bearman chose 87 as his permanent racing number for [[Formula One]], as it was the number that he first used in [[kart racing]].<ref name="F1number">{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/bearman-explains-f1-race-number-choice-as-he-reveals-amazing-hamilton-video/10631139/ |title=Bearman explains F1 race number choice, reveals "amazing" Hamilton video |last=Noble |first=Jonathan |date=4 July 2024 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=25 January 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240926160931/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/bearman-explains-f1-race-number-choice-as-he-reveals-amazing-hamilton-video/10631139/ |archive-date=26 September 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref>

== Junior racing career ==
=== Karting (2013–2020) ===
Bearman started karting competitively in 2013, when he raced in the championship of the Trent Valley Kart Club. He then moved to compete in the [[Super 1 National Kart Championships|Super 1 National Championships]], where he managed a best finish of second in 2016 and 2017, driving in the Cadet category.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Super 1 National Honda Cadet Championship 2016 standings {{!}} Driver Database |url=https://www.driverdb.com/championships/standings/super-1-national-honda-cadet-championship/2016/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602212822/https://www.driverdb.com/championships/standings/super-1-national-honda-cadet-championship/2016/ |archive-date=2 June 2021 |access-date=29 May 2021 |website=[[DriverDB.com]]}}</ref> He then won the Kartmasters British Grand Prix in 2017,<ref>{{Cite web|title=2017 Kartmasters British GP - Honda Cadet|url=https://www.driverdb.com/championships/kartmasters-british-grand-prix---honda-cadet/2017|access-date=21 January 2025|website=DriverDB|language=en}}</ref> and he finished his karting career off strongly in 2019 with victory in the IAME International Final, IAME Euro Series and IAME Winter Cup.<ref>{{Cite web |title=IAME International Final - X30 Junior 2019 standings {{!}} Driver Database |url=https://www.driverdb.com/championships/standings/iame-international-final---x30-junior/2019/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602212604/https://www.driverdb.com/championships/standings/iame-international-final---x30-junior/2019/ |archive-date=2 June 2021 |access-date=29 May 2021 |website=[[DriverDB.com]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Ollie Bearman {{!}} British Racing Driver {{!}} Formula 4 |url=https://www.olliebearman.com/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210516213759/https://www.olliebearman.com/ |archive-date=16 May 2021 |access-date=29 May 2021 |website=Ollie Bearman |language=en-GB}}</ref> Bearman also won the IAME Winter Cup and the Euro Series in the X30 Senior Category during 2020.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2020 IAME Winter Cup - X30 Senior|url=https://www.driverdb.com/championships/iame-winter-cup-x30-senior/2020|access-date=21 January 2025|website=DriverDB|language=en}}</ref>

=== Formula 4 (2020–2021) ===
==== 2020: Junior formulae debut ====
In 2020, Bearman made his single-seater debut in the [[2020 ADAC Formula 4 Championship|ADAC Formula 4 Championship]] with [[US Racing]], whilst also racing in three rounds of [[2020 Italian F4 Championship|Italian F4]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=27 July 2020 |title=Ollie Bearman to race in ADAC F4 opener with US Racing |url=https://formulascout.com/ollie-bearman-to-race-in-adac-f4-opener-with-us-racing/65103 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210201204111/https://formulascout.com/ollie-bearman-to-race-in-adac-f4-opener-with-us-racing/65103 |archive-date=1 February 2021 |access-date=29 May 2021 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> His campaign in the German series started off with regular points finishes in the first two rounds,<ref>{{Cite web|date=3 August 2020|title=The new stars who stood out on a big Formula 4 weekend|url=https://formulascout.com/the-new-stars-who-stood-out-on-a-big-formula-4-weekend/65723|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> before achieving his debut victory at the [[Hockenheimring]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Erlösung für Bearman - Zweiter Sieg für Dürksen: Erster Sieg in der ADAC Formel 4 für Oliver Bearman auf dem Hockenheimring {{!}} ADAC Formel 4 |url=https://www.adac-motorsport.de/adac-formel-4/news/2020/erlosung-fur-bearman-zweiter-sieg-fur-durksen-erster-sieg-in-der-adac-formel-4-fur-oliver-bearman-auf-dem-hockenheimring |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220827153624/https://www.adac-motorsport.de/adac-formel-4/news/2020/erlosung-fur-bearman-zweiter-sieg-fur-durksen-erster-sieg-in-der-adac-formel-4-fur-oliver-bearman-auf-dem-hockenheimring |archive-date=27 August 2022 |access-date=27 August 2022 |website=www.adac-motorsport.de |language=de}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Waring |first=Bethonie |date=19 September 2020 |title=Briton Ollie Bearman seizes maiden F4 win at Hockenheim |url=https://formulascout.com/briton-ollie-bearman-seizes-maiden-f4-win-at-hockenheim/68323 |access-date=29 May 2021 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> Bearman followed that up by scoring two further podiums, one at the [[Nürburgring]] and [[Motorsport Arena Oschersleben|Oschersleben]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Waring|first=Bethonie|date=26 September 2020|title=Edgar takes Nurburgring ADAC F4 victory in mixed conditions|url=https://formulascout.com/edgar-takes-nurburgring-adac-f4-victory-in-mixed-conditions/68618|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Allen|first=Peter|date=8 December 2020|title=Crawford resists Edgar in penultimate race to close on ADAC F4 title|url=https://formulascout.com/crawford-resists-edgar-in-penultimate-race-to-close-on-adac-f4-title/70661|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> Bearman finished seventh in the standings with 144 points, ahead of fellow rookie teammate [[Vladislav Lomko]] but behind top rookie and teammate [[Tim Tramnitz]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=ADAC Formula 4 Standings 2020 {{!}} Motorsport Stats |url=https://motorsportstats.com/series/ADAC%20Formula%204/standings/2020 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220827153624/https://motorsportstats.com/series/ADAC%20Formula%204/standings/2020 |archive-date=27 August 2022 |access-date=27 August 2022 |website=motorsportstats.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=23 December 2020 |title=The standout Formula 4 drivers around the world in 2020 |url=https://formulascout.com/the-standout-formula-4-drivers-around-the-world-in-2020/73020 |access-date=29 May 2021 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> In his appearances in the Italian Championship, Bearman scored a total of two podiums, with one of them being a race win in [[ACI Vallelunga Circuit|Vallelunga]], leading to him finishing tenth in the end results.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=5 December 2020 |title=Bearman wins safety car-filled Italian F4 opener at Vallelunga |url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-wins-safety-car-filled-italian-f4-opener-at-vallelunga/72126 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210204204439/https://formulascout.com/bearman-wins-safety-car-filled-italian-f4-opener-at-vallelunga/72126 |archive-date=4 February 2021 |access-date=29 May 2021 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref>

==== 2021: Maiden championships ====
[[File:F4 Italy 2021 Spielberg Nr. 87 Bearman.jpg|thumb|left|Bearman racing in the [[2021 Italian F4 Championship]]]]
For the 2021 season, Bearman switched to [[Van Amersfoort Racing]] to perform double duties in both the [[2021 ADAC Formula 4 Championship|German]] and [[2021 Italian F4 Championship|Italian F4]] Championships.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=26 January 2021 |title=Bearman switches to Van Amersfoort Racing for second year in F4 |url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-switches-to-van-amersfoort-racing-for-second-year-in-f4/74508 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210306234952/https://formulascout.com/bearman-switches-to-van-amersfoort-racing-for-second-year-in-f4/74508 |archive-date=6 March 2021 |access-date=29 May 2021 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> In the Italian series, the Brit kicked off his season with a third place at the [[Circuit Paul Ricard]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=15 May 2021|title=Smal starts Italian F4 season with Paul Ricard victory|url=https://formulascout.com/smal-starts-italian-f4-season-with-paul-ricard-victory/78739|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> Following another podium in the same round, Bearman went on a podium and win streak, which lasted for nine and seven races respectively.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=16 May 2021|title=Tramnitz controls third Italian F4 race at Paul Ricard to build points lead|url=https://formulascout.com/tramnitz-controls-third-italian-f4-race-at-paul-ricard-to-build-points-lead/78808|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> This included two victories in [[Misano World Circuit Marco Simoncelli|Misano]],<ref>{{Cite web|last=Waring|first=Bethonie|date=5 June 2021|title=Bearman moves into Italian F4 lead with Misano win|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-moves-into-italian-f4-lead-with-misano-win/79644|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Waring|first=Bethonie|date=6 June 2021|title=Bearman extends Italian F4 lead with back-to-back Misano wins|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-extends-italian-f4-lead-with-back-to-back-misano-wins/79663|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> a hat-trick of wins at the [[Vallelunga Circuit]] and two wins in [[Imola Circuit|Imola]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Woollard|first=Craig|date=27 June 2021|title=Bearman makes it five wins in a row in restarted Italian F4 race|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-makes-it-five-wins-in-a-row-in-restarted-italian-f4-race/80490|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=24 July 2021 |title=Bearman wins, title rivals retire in Italian F4's Imola opener |url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-wins-title-rivals-retire-in-italian-f4s-imola-opener/81726 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211010145016/https://formulascout.com/bearman-wins-title-rivals-retire-in-italian-f4s-imola-opener/81726 |archive-date=10 October 2021 |access-date=10 October 2021 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=25 July 2021 |title=Bearman extends Italian F4 lead to over 100 points with Imola win |url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-extends-italian-f4-lead-to-over-100-points-with-imola-win/81765 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211010145017/https://formulascout.com/bearman-extends-italian-f4-lead-to-over-100-points-with-imola-win/81765 |archive-date=10 October 2021 |access-date=10 October 2021 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> However, a disqualification from the third Imola race for an engine irregularity meant that Bearman lost his streak, having originally won the race.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=2 August 2021 |title=Bearman excluded from F4 win at Imola for non-compliant engine |url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-excluded-from-f4-win-at-imola-for-non-compliant-engine/82135 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211010145019/https://formulascout.com/bearman-excluded-from-f4-win-at-imola-for-non-compliant-engine/82135 |archive-date=10 October 2021 |access-date=10 October 2021 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> Undeterred, Bearman achieved his eighth win of the season at the following race at the [[Red Bull Ring]], and followed it up with another podium in the second race.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Bearman and double for Tramnitz at the Red Bull Ring in round 5 of the Italian F.4 Championship Powered by Abarth |url=https://nocache.media.stellantis.com/em-en/abarth/press/bearman-and-double-for-tramnitz-at-the-red-bull-ring-in-round-5-of-the-italian-f-4-championship-powered-by-abarth |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220827155130/https://nocache.media.stellantis.com/em-en/abarth/press/bearman-and-double-for-tramnitz-at-the-red-bull-ring-in-round-5-of-the-italian-f-4-championship-powered-by-abarth |archive-date=27 August 2022 |access-date=27 August 2022 |website=nocache.media.stellantis.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=12 September 2021|title=Tramnitz marvels in wild and wet Italian F4 race at Red Bull Ring|url=https://formulascout.com/tramnitz-marvels-in-wild-and-wet-italian-f4-race-at-red-bull-ring/83687|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> In the penultimate round of the season in [[Mugello Circuit|Mugello]], despite not scoring any podiums, Bearman won the title with a tenth place in the third race, putting the championship out of reach for his closest rival [[Tim Tramnitz]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 November 2021 |title=Exclusive: Ollie Bearman 'hoping to make positive impact' as he looks to secure 2022 FIA F3 Prema seat |url=https://f1feederseries.com/2021/11/04/ollie-bearman-hoping-to-make-positive-impact-as-he-looks-to-secure-2022-fia-f3-prema-seat/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220827153624/https://f1feederseries.com/2021/11/04/ollie-bearman-hoping-to-make-positive-impact-as-he-looks-to-secure-2022-fia-f3-prema-seat/ |archive-date=27 August 2022 |access-date=27 August 2022 |website=F1 Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref> He rounded out his campaign in perfect style, winning all three rounds during the season finale in [[Monza Circuit|Monza]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Gascoigne|first=Roger|date=30 October 2021|title=Bearman takes thrilling win from Antonelli at Monza in Italian F4|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-takes-thrilling-win-from-antonelli-at-monza-in-italian-f4/85948|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Gascoigne|first=Roger|date=30 October 2021|title=Bearman wins again at Monza as late safety car thwarts Antonelli|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-wins-again-at-monza-as-late-safety-car-thwarts-antonelli/86016|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Gascoigne|first=Roger|date=31 October 2021|title=Flawless Bearman completes Monza hat-trick in Italian F4 finale|url=https://formulascout.com/flawless-bearman-completes-monza-hat-trick-in-italian-f4-finale/86040|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> Bearman had dominated the season with eleven wins, fifteen podiums and 343 points, 111 ahead of his nearest rival.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Gascoigne|first=Roger|date=4 November 2021|title=Paddock round-up: FREC and F4 in Monza, and a failed Festival defence|url=https://formulascout.com/paddock-round-up-frec-and-f4-in-monza-and-a-failed-festival-defence/86172|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref>

[[File:F4 Deutschland 2021 Spielberg Nr. 87 Bearman 2.jpg|thumb|Bearman racing in the [[2021 ADAC Formula 4 Championship]]]]
In the German championship, Bearman started the season with a double victory in the opening round at the [[Red Bull Ring]],<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=12 June 2021|title=Bearman controls ADAC F4 opener ahead of frantic battles for points|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-controls-adac-f4-opener-ahead-of-frantic-battles-for-points/79835|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Allen|first=Peter|date=12 June 2021|title=Bearman doubles up in ADAC F4 opener at Red Bull Ring|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-doubles-up-in-adac-f4-opener-at-red-bull-ring/79859|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> although a collision with [[Luke Browning]] on the opening lap in Race 3 prevented a clean sweep.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=13 June 2021|title=Browning wins dramatic ADAC F4 race after Montoya gets penalty|url=https://formulascout.com/browning-wins-dramatic-adac-f4-race-after-montoya-gets-penalty/79872|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> He emulated his feat the next round in [[Circuit Zandvoort|Zandvoort]], securing another double victory.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Waring|first=Bethonie|date=10 July 2021|title=Bearman beats Montoya to win again in ADAC F4 Zandvoort opener|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-beats-montoya-to-win-again-in-adac-f4-zandvoort-opener/81023|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Waring|first=Bethonie|date=11 July 2021|title=Bearman wins again at Zandvoort after safety car restart crash|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-wins-again-at-zandvoort-after-safety-car-restart-crash/81064|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> He took another win at [[Hockenheimring|Hockenheim]],<ref>{{Cite web|last=Gascoigne|first=Roger|date=18 September 2021|title=Bearman holds off US Racing trio to win ADAC F4 Hockenheim race one|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-holds-off-us-racing-trio-to-win-adac-f4-hockenheim-race-one/83913|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> and despite four more podiums in the next two rounds, title rival Tramnitz closed the gap with three wins.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Gascoigne|first=Roger|date=24 October 2021|title=Browning holds off Dufek to win third ADAC F4 race at Hockenheim|url=https://formulascout.com/browning-holds-off-dufek-to-win-third-adac-f4-race-at-hockenheim/85657|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> In the [[Nürburgring]] finale, he won the second race,<ref>{{Cite web|last=Gascoigne|first=Roger|date=7 November 2021|title=Dominant Bearman wins at wet Nurburgring to close on ADAC F4 title|url=https://formulascout.com/dominant-bearman-wins-at-wet-nurburgring-to-close-on-adac-f4-title/86372|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> and a fourth place on Race 3 allowed Bearman to secure the ADAC F4 crown.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Gascoigne|first=Roger|date=7 November 2021|title=Bearman and VAR take ADAC F4 titles as Bedrin wins season finale|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-takes-adac-f4-title-as-bedrin-wins-season-finale/86409|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> It was another outstanding season for Bearman, taking six wins, eleven podiums and 295 points on route to becoming the first driver to win two successive Formula 4 titles in one year.<ref>{{Cite web |date=11 November 2021 |title=OLIVER BEARMAN: DER CHAMPION DER ADAC FORMEL 4 IM PORTRÄT |url=https://www.motorsport-xl.de/news/2021/Formel-4/Oliver-Bearman-Der-Champion-der-ADAC-Formel-4-im-Portraet-44356.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230602120130/https://www.motorsport-xl.de/news/2021/Formel-4/Oliver-Bearman-Der-Champion-der-ADAC-Formel-4-im-Portraet-44356.html |archive-date=2 June 2023 |access-date=27 August 2022 |website=Motorsport XL}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Gascoigne|first=Roger|date=20 December 2021|title=The route Bearman took to his momentous F4 title double|url=https://formulascout.com/the-route-bearman-took-to-his-momentous-f4-title-double/87620|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref>

In September 2021, as a reward for his two F4 titles, Bearman was nominated for the [[Autosport BRDC Award]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=30 September 2021 |title=FOUR FINALISTS SELECTED FOR 2021 ASTON MARTIN AUTOSPORT BRDC AWARD |url=http://www.brdc.co.uk/Four-Finalists-Selected-for-2021-Aston-Martin-Autosport-BRDC-Award |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220405062917/http://www.brdc.co.uk/Four-Finalists-Selected-for-2021-Aston-Martin-Autosport-BRDC-Award |archive-date=5 April 2022 |access-date=7 February 2022 |website=British Racing Drivers' Club}}</ref> Additionally, in December 2021, Bearman was awarded the [[Henry Surtees#Henry Surtees Award|Henry Surtees Award]] for most outstanding performance by a BRDC rising star.<ref>{{Cite web |date=20 December 2021 |title=2021 BRDC ANNUAL AWARD WINNERS ANNOUNCED |url=http://www.brdc.co.uk/2021-BRDC-Annual-Award-Winners-Announced |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220207153618/http://www.brdc.co.uk/2021-BRDC-Annual-Award-Winners-Announced |archive-date=7 February 2022 |access-date=7 February 2022 |website=British Racing Drivers' Club}}</ref>

=== Formula Three (2021–2022) ===
==== 2021 ====
[[File:OliverBearmanF3.png|thumb|left|Bearman at Brands Hatch in 2021]]
Along with his duties in Formula 4, Bearman raced in the [[2021 GB3 Championship|GB3 Championship]] with [[Fortec Motorsport]]s, partnering [[Roberto Faria]] and [[Mikkel Grundtvig]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=18 May 2021 |title=F4 star Ollie Bearman adds BRDC British F3 programme with Fortec |url=https://formulascout.com/f4-star-ollie-bearman-adds-brdc-british-f3-programme-with-fortec/78853 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602214330/https://formulascout.com/f4-star-ollie-bearman-adds-brdc-british-f3-programme-with-fortec/78853 |archive-date=2 June 2021 |access-date=29 May 2021 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> He started his campaign off strongly, scoring two second-place finishes in the first two races at [[Brands Hatch]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Whitfield |first=Steve |date=22 May 2021 |title=Simmons beats Bearman to victory in BRDC British F3 season opener |url=https://formulascout.com/simmons-beats-bearman-to-victory-in-brdc-british-f3-season-opener/79119 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602214540/https://formulascout.com/simmons-beats-bearman-to-victory-in-brdc-british-f3-season-opener/79119 |archive-date=2 June 2021 |access-date=29 May 2021 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Whitfield|first=Steve|date=23 May 2021|title=O'Sullivan wins British F3 Brands Hatch race two, Simmons out in crash|url=https://formulascout.com/osullivan-wins-british-f3-brands-hatch-race-two-simmons-out-in-crash/79179|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> Having skipped the following three rounds in order to concentrate on his F4 campaign, Bearman came back at the [[Snetterton Circuit]],<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=3 August 2021|title=Bearman and Lubin back on GB3 grid for Snetterton this weekend|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-and-lubin-back-on-gb3-grid-for-snetterton-this-weekend/82162|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> where he won the opening race,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Callander |first=Michael |date=7 August 2021 |title=Bearman wins Race 1 as GB3 takes on Snetterton 300 |url=https://www.thecheckeredflag.co.uk/2021/08/bearman-wins-race-1-as-gb3-takes-on-snetterton-300/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220827151126/https://www.thecheckeredflag.co.uk/2021/08/bearman-wins-race-1-as-gb3-takes-on-snetterton-300/ |archive-date=27 August 2022 |access-date=27 August 2022 |website=The Checkered Flag |language=en-GB}}</ref> and he followed that up by qualifying on pole for the first race at [[Silverstone Circuit|Silverstone]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=GB3 QUALIFYING: Bearman and Simmons claim Silverstone poles |url=https://news.msv.com/25516.aspx |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220827151132/https://news.msv.com/25516.aspx |archive-date=27 August 2022 |access-date=27 August 2022 |website=news.msv.com}}</ref> However, his chances of victory were slashed after losing his front left wheel on the second lap,<ref>{{Cite web|last=Whitfield|first=Steve|date=14 August 2021|title=Simmons wins, Bearman loses wheel in GB3 race one at Silverstone|url=https://formulascout.com/simmons-wins-bearman-loses-wheel-in-gb3-race-one-at-silverstone/82445|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> which meant that a second place in Race 2 was the highest finish of his weekend.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Whitfield|first=Steve|date=15 August 2021|title=Simmons beats Bearman to GB3 race two win at Silverstone|url=https://formulascout.com/simmons-beats-bearman-to-gb3-race-two-win-at-silverstone/82473|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> Bearman did not take part in any more rounds following that and he finished 14th in the standings, with 163 points.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Whitfield|first=Steve|date=9 November 2021|title=GB3 season review: Catching up with runaway champion Zak O'Sullivan|url=https://formulascout.com/gb3-season-review-catching-up-with-runaway-champion-zak-osullivan/86240|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref>

==== 2022 ====
===== Formula Regional =====
In the winter of 2022, Bearman signed with [[Mumbai Falcons]] to partake in the final two rounds of the [[2022 Formula Regional Asian Championship|Formula Regional Asian Championship]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=10 January 2022|title=Mumbai Falcons gets three Ferrari juniors and Montoya for FRAC|url=https://formulascout.com/mumbai-falcons-announces-three-ferrari-juniors-and-montoya-for-frac/88402|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> His main highlight was a podium in only his second race at the [[Dubai Autodrome]], and with two other points finishes, he placed 15th in the standings.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Edwards|first=Jordan|date=13 February 2022|title=Pasma wins in FRAC as Crawford storms up order to second|url=https://formulascout.com/patrik-pasma-takes-win-as-crawford-storms-up-the-order/89626|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Paul Aron is back: 5 takeaways from FRAC Round 4 at Dubai|date=14 February 2022|url=https://feederseries.net/2022/02/14/paul-aron-is-back-5-takeaways-from-frac-round-4-at-dubai/|access-date=21 January 2025|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref>

===== FIA Formula 3 =====
[[File:FIA F3 Austria 2022 Nr. 6 Bearman.jpg|thumb|Bearman driving the [[Dallara F3 2019]] during the [[2022 Spielberg Formula 3 round]]]]
On 31 October 2021, Bearman was announced to be participating in the post-season test of the [[2021 FIA Formula 3 Championship|FIA Formula 3 Championship]] with [[Prema Racing]], partnering [[Jak Crawford]], [[Arthur Leclerc]] and [[Paul Aron]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gascoigne |first=Roger |date=31 October 2021 |title=Crawford and Bearman join Prema for FIA F3 Valencia post-season test |url=https://formulascout.com/crawford-and-bearman-join-prema-for-fia-f3-valencia-post-season-test/86076 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230813200938/https://formulascout.com/crawford-and-bearman-join-prema-for-fia-f3-valencia-post-season-test/86076 |archive-date=13 August 2023 |access-date=7 November 2021 |website=Formula Scout}}</ref> At the end of the year, Bearman was announced to be driving with Prema for the [[2022 FIA Formula 3 Championship|2022 season]] alongside Crawford and Leclerc.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gascoigne |first=Roger |date=28 December 2021 |title=Bearman to join Prema for 2022 FIA F3 Championship season |url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/ukGQCcklecDFVu8PI7vHM/prema-racing-sign-ferrari-junior-bearman-for-2022 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211228130824/https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/ukGQCcklecDFVu8PI7vHM/prema-racing-sign-ferrari-junior-bearman-for-2022 |archive-date=28 December 2021 |access-date=28 December 2021 |website=FIA Formula 3 Championship}}</ref>

Bearman started his season by controlling the first race of the year in [[2022 Sakhir Formula 3 round|Bahrain]], although, having crossed the finish line in first place, he was issued a penalty for multiple track limits breaches, which demoted him to second behind [[Isack Hadjar]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=2022 Bahrain F3 Sprint Race report and highlights: Hadjar wins on debut after Bearman handed penalty {{!}} Formula 1® |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.f3-hadjar-wins-on-debut-after-bearman-handed-penalty.5RCHenr9B9PqL89QMANBNn.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220827121448/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.f3-hadjar-wins-on-debut-after-bearman-handed-penalty.5RCHenr9B9PqL89QMANBNn.html |archive-date=27 August 2022 |access-date=27 August 2022 |website=www.formula1.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=2022 Round 1 post-Sprint Race press conference|date=19 March 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/4TbLmLtxm24J3vCDFq18D6/2022-round-1-post-sprint-race-press-conference|access-date=21 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> He followed it up with a strong sixth place in the feature race.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Formula 3: Academy drivers on the podium: Bearman second on his debut, Leclerc stages a thrilling fightback|date=20 March 2022|url=https://www.ferrari.com/en-EN/fda/articles/formula-3-academy-drivers-on-the-podium-bearman-second-on-his-debut-leclerc-stages-a-thrilling-fightback|access-date=21 January 2025|website=[[Scuderia Ferrari]]|language=en}}</ref> This was followed by a disappointing event at [[2022 Imola Formula 3 round|Imola]]; there, having been denied a points finish in the first race due to a spin that had come as a direct result of teammate Leclerc pushing him onto the grass,<ref>{{Citation |title=F3 Sprint Race Highlights {{!}} 2022 Emilia Romagna Grand Prix |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GZ561yD5rGY |access-date=27 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230420045626/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GZ561yD5rGY&feature=youtu.be |archive-date=20 April 2023 |url-status=live |language=en}}</ref> Bearman was battling to remain in third place near the end of Sunday's feature race. On the final lap, Bearman collided with [[Grégoire Saucy]] at the penultimate corner,<ref>{{Cite web|title=FEATURE RACE: Stanek stands tall to win dramatic Formula 3 Feature Race|date=24 April 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/7kh76v3gC87a7MlxRc1iei/feature-race-stanek-stands-tall-to-win-dramatic-formula-3-feature-race|access-date=21 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> which sent the Swiss driver out of the race and caused Bearman to be demoted from fourth to 17th post-race.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Imola Feature Race penalties|date=24 April 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/1ngjcLVzXDQ2x3km5uwWYZ/imola-feature-race-penalties|access-date=21 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> The next round in [[2022 Barcelona Formula 3 round|Barcelona]] panned out more quietly, scoring a fifth place during the feature race.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Formula 3 - Points for Leclerc and Bearman|date=22 May 2022|url=https://www.ferrari.com/en-EN/fda/articles/formula-3-points-for-leclerc-and-bearman|access-date=21 January 2025|website=[[Scuderia Ferrari]]|language=en}}</ref>

Bearman gained form in the subsequent three rounds, starting from [[2022 Silverstone Formula 3 round|Silverstone]], where from sixth, Bearman made a penultimate lap pass on [[Caio Collet]] for the rostrum places before battling his compatriot [[Zak O'Sullivan]] to the line for second; nevertheless it was Bearman's first feature race podium.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=4 July 2022|title=Bearman: "Very lucky" to finish F3 feature race "without any incident"|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-very-lucky-to-finish-f3-feature-race-without-any-incident/95861|access-date=22 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> Bearman then qualified third in [[2022 Spielberg Formula 3 round|Austria]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=2022 Round 5 post-Qualifying press conference|date=8 July 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/2vgiCezMpkvVQrsy3mw4LH/2022-round-5-post-qualifying-press-conference-f3|access-date=22 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> He lost a few places after a slight contact with [[Zane Maloney]] mid-race, but eventually finished in sixth place, only to be dropped to 16th due to track limits.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Collet says DRS 'plays a big role' at Red Bull Ring as Crawford scores maiden FIA F3 win|date=9 July 2022|url=https://feederseries.net/2022/07/09/collet-says-drs-plays-a-big-role-at-red-bull-ring-as-crawford-scores-maiden-fia-f3-win/|access-date=22 January 2025|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Formula 3: Olier Bearman on the podium in Spielberg|date=10 July 2022|url=https://www.ferrari.com/en-EN/fda/articles/formula-3-oliver-bearman-on-the-podium-in-spielberg|access-date=22 January 2025|website=[[Scuderia Ferrari]]|language=en|archive-date=27 August 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220827150600/https://www.ferrari.com/en-EN/fda/articles/formula-3-oliver-bearman-on-the-podium-in-spielberg|url-status=dead}}</ref> In a damp feature race, Bearman remained in his position to secure another third place podium.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2022 Round 5 post-Feature Race press conference|date=10 July 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/4WbbCbz6jPQLbdyYYw9RTc/2022-round-5-post-feature-race-press-conference-f2|access-date=22 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> Bearman qualified third in [[2022 Budapest Formula 3 round|Hungary]] for the second successive round.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2022 Round 6 post-Qualifying press conference|date=29 July 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/3dGtMpeBHCyrS4FC842QGR/2022-round-6-post-qualifying-press-conference-f3|access-date=22 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> After finishing fifth in the sprint race,<ref>{{Cite web|title=R06 Hungaroring - FIA Formula 3 Race 1 Report|date=31 July 2022|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/18986-r06-hungaroring-fia-formula-3-race-1-report|access-date=22 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Bearman secured yet another third place during the feature race, as he narrowly missed out on pipping Maloney for second by 0.025s.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2022 Round 6 Feature Race: Thoughts from the top 3|date=31 July 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/77j5en5LRxz27IKHc2eOnE/2022-round-6-feature-race-thoughts-from-the-top-3|access-date=22 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref>

Following the summer break in [[2022 Spa-Francorchamps Formula 3 round|Spa-Francorchamps]], Bearman was able to fight his way to the front during the opening embers of the sprint race, having started from fifth, and took his first victory in the category despite a pair of [[safety car]]s and a Red flag interruption interfering with his race.<ref>{{Cite web |title=First Formula 3 win for Oliver Bearman |url=https://www.ferrari.com/en-EN/fda/articles/spa-first-formula-3-win-for-oliver-bearman |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220827150601/https://www.ferrari.com/en-EN/fda/articles/spa-first-formula-3-win-for-oliver-bearman |archive-date=27 August 2022 |access-date=27 August 2022 |website=www.ferrari.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=27 August 2022 |title=F3 Spa: Bearman clinches maiden win amid chaotic sprint race |url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/f3-spa-bearman-clinches-maiden-win-amid-chaotic-sprint-race/10358786/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220827102545/https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/f3-spa-bearman-clinches-maiden-win-amid-chaotic-sprint-race/10358786/ |archive-date=27 August 2022 |access-date=27 August 2022 |website=www.autosport.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Alonso Lopez|first=Alejandro|date=27 August 2022|title=Escaping DRS range after restarts "key" to Bearman's first F3 win|url=https://formulascout.com/escaping-drs-range-after-restarts-key-to-bearmans-first-f3-win/97774|access-date=22 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> The following day, Bearman once again finished third in the feature race, having overtaken [[Oliver Goethe]] on the final lap.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2022 Round 7 Feature Race: Thoughts from the top 3|date=28 August 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/3Z6R8DMf3bsK8BmSbXbid1/2022-round-7-feature-race-thoughts-from-the-top-3|access-date=22 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Bearman's Guest Column: Finally a chance to prove my pace|date=30 August 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/3noLb609fTJz1E37M9DW8B/bearmans-guest-column-finally-a-chance-to-prove-my-pace|access-date=22 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> Misfortune followed in [[2022 Zandvoort Formula 3 round|Zandvoort]], as a red flag hampered Bearman's qualifying efforts, leaving the Brit 14th on the grid.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R08 Zandvoort - FIA Formula 3 Qualifying Report|date=3 September 2022|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19006-r08-zandvoort-fia-formula-3-qualifying-report|access-date=22 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> In the sprint race, Bearman moved up to tenth but made a mistake and lost the position to [[Roman Staněk]], finishing in 11th.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R08 Zandvoort - FIA Formula 3 Race 1 Report|date=4 September 2022|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19008-r08-zandvoort-fia-formula-3-race-1-report|access-date=22 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> During the feature race, a penalty for a collision with O'Sullivan meant that Bearman lost his tenth place again, not adding points to his tally.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Round 8 post-Feature Race penalties|date=4 September 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/4ss8HuOkDAtFNJMs2KLk0J/round-8-post-feature-race-penalties|access-date=22 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> Undeterred by his slim title chances going into the season finale at [[2022 Monza Formula 3 round|Monza]],<ref>{{Cite web|title=Bearman on F3 title showdown: 'Keep a cool head and no silly risks'|date=6 September 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/2EN2RmzZ1NVxOUoBFmUuwj/bearman-on-f3-title-showdown-keep-a-cool-head-and-no-silly-risks|access-date=22 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> Bearman qualified in sixth.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R09 - Monza - FIA Formula 3 Qualifying Report|date=10 September 2022|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19017-r09-monza-fia-formula-3-qualifying-report|access-date=22 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> In the sprint race, Bearman finished second in the sprint race courtesy of a double-overtake on [[Jonny Edgar]] and [[Caio Collet]] into the first chicane, and even almost snatched the win from [[Franco Colapinto]] on the last lap.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2022 Round 9 post-Sprint Race press conference|date=10 September 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/r9hvr2W86dpQWUZol5vqv/2022-round-9-post-sprint-race-press-conference-f3|access-date=22 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> He continued his fight on Sunday, battling for the lead with [[Zane Maloney]] before a red flag ended the race prematurely, meaning Bearman finished the race in second place.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2022 Round 9 post-Feature Race press conference|date=11 September 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/14NWZC7cWnAg2Jfzlu3qQ3/2022-round-9-post-feature-race-press-conference-f3|access-date=22 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> With one win, eight podiums and 132 points, Bearman finished third in the standings, a mere seven points behind champion [[Victor Martins]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Evolving from rookie to title protagonist, now Oliver Bearman's coming of age|date=5 October 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/6evJdoM3bHnMYe5sOJN8BD/evolving-from-rookie-to-title-protagonist-now-oliver-bearmans-coming-of-age|access-date=22 January 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> Despite being regretful of "all the races where [he] needlessly lost points", the Briton maintained that he was happy to finish third in the championship.<ref>{{Cite web |date=21 October 2022 |title=How Ferrari rising star Bearman fared in his maiden FIA F3 season |url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/how-ferraris-british-rising-star-bearman-fared-in-his-maiden-fia-f3-season/10387023/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221121143934/https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/how-ferraris-british-rising-star-bearman-fared-in-his-maiden-fia-f3-season/10387023/ |archive-date=21 November 2022 |access-date=21 November 2022 |website=[[Autosport.com]] |language=en}}</ref>

=== FIA Formula 2 (2023–2024) ===
==== 2023 ====
[[File:FIA F2 Austria 2023 Nr. 8 Bearman (1).jpg|thumb|left|Bearman driving the [[Dallara F2 2018]] during the [[2023 Spielberg Formula 2 round]]]]
On 14 November 2022, Bearman was announced as a [[Prema Powerteam|Prema Racing]] driver for the [[2023 Formula 2 Championship]], partnering [[Mercedes Junior Team|Mercedes junior]] [[Frederik Vesti]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=14 November 2022 |title=Bearman promoted to Formula 2 with PREMA Racing for 2023 |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/6fTPWwatSHb2h6h8vUypER/bearman-promoted-to-formula-2-with-prema-racing-for-2022 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230309125215/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/6fTPWwatSHb2h6h8vUypER/bearman-promoted-to-formula-2-with-prema-racing-for-2022 |archive-date=9 March 2023 |access-date=14 November 2022 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website}}</ref> Bearman started his season in [[2023 Sakhir Formula 2 round|Bahrain]] with 12th in qualifying,<ref>{{Cite web|title=R01 Bahrain - FIA Formula 2 Qualifying Report|date=3 March 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19075-r01-bahrain-fia-formula-2-qualifying-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> but could not salvage much in the sprint race, finishing P15.<ref>{{Cite web |date=5 March 2023 |title=R01 Bahrain - FIA Formula 2 Race 1 Report |url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19077-r01-bahrain-fia-formula-2-race-1-report |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230308123132/https://premaracing.com/en/news/19077-r01-bahrain-fia-formula-2-race-1-report |archive-date=8 March 2023 |access-date=9 March 2023 |website=[[Prema Powerteam]] |language=en}}</ref> Taking advantage of lap 1 chaos in the feature race, Bearman rose to fourth early on. However, tyre degradation proved to be a factor as he was among the first to pit, and fell down the order late on for a disappointing 14th place.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Alonso Lopez |first=Alejandro |date=17 March 2023 |title=Tyre degradation struggle of F2 debut "a one-off thing", hopes Bearman |url=https://formulascout.com/tyre-degradation-struggles-a-one-off-thing-bearman-hopes/104710 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230326052810/https://formulascout.com/tyre-degradation-struggles-a-one-off-thing-bearman-hopes/104710 |archive-date=26 March 2023 |access-date=26 March 2023 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-GB}}</ref> In [[2023 Jeddah Formula 2 round|Jeddah]], the Briton [[:Wiktionary:break one's duck|broke his duck]] and qualified second having topped practice.<ref>{{Cite web |date=17 March 2023 |title=Bearman relishing the adrenaline rush after confidence-boosting Free Practice |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/6WxfckIGOlyoRwhTPYly5M/bearman-relishing-the-adrenaline-rush-after-confidence-boosting-free |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230326001107/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/6WxfckIGOlyoRwhTPYly5M/bearman-relishing-the-adrenaline-rush-after-confidence-boosting-free |archive-date=26 March 2023 |access-date=26 March 2023 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=17 March 2023 |title=2023 Round 2 post-Qualifying press conference |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/2X0YnbyyATaoTkc78tv7WE/2023-round-2-post-qualifying-press-conference |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230325234148/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/2X0YnbyyATaoTkc78tv7WE/2023-round-2-post-qualifying-press-conference |archive-date=25 March 2023 |access-date=26 March 2023 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref> However, his sprint race ended after [[Théo Pourchaire]] braked late and slammed into him, which ended both their races.<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 March 2023 |title=SPRINT RACE: Iwasa holds his nerve in Jeddah masterclass |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/201gdTC2D3qbF1QlNGIMiJ/sprint-race-iwasa-holds-his-nerve-in-jeddah-masterclass |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230325234552/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/201gdTC2D3qbF1QlNGIMiJ/sprint-race-iwasa-holds-his-nerve-in-jeddah-masterclass |archive-date=25 March 2023 |access-date=26 March 2023 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref> In the feature race, Bearman battled with [[Victor Martins]] early on after seizing the lead at the start. However Bearman spun on his own later on, which dropped him down the order, and he subsequently lost more positions, ultimately finishing in tenth place.<ref>{{Cite web |date=20 March 2023 |title=René Rosin: Jeddah performances prove it's 'game on' for PREMA in 2023 |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/4K1GouKm8CdGfNozQGLUoy/rene-rosin-jeddah-performances-prove-its-game-on-for-prema-in-2023 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230326055810/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/4K1GouKm8CdGfNozQGLUoy/rene-rosin-jeddah-performances-prove-its-game-on-for-prema-in-2023 |archive-date=26 March 2023 |access-date=26 March 2023 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref>

Bearman ended sixth in qualifying at [[2023 Melbourne Formula 2 round|Melbourne]], despite an early crash.<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 March 2023 |title=Bearman aiming to eliminate mistakes after Qualifying turnaround |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/2549FTzccT60eIyBMhmgb0/bearman-aiming-to-eliminate-mistakes-after-qualifying-turnaround |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230409053043/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/2549FTzccT60eIyBMhmgb0/bearman-aiming-to-eliminate-mistakes-after-qualifying-turnaround |archive-date=9 April 2023 |access-date=9 April 2023 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref> In a sprint race where he battled many of his rivals, he secured seventh.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R03 Melbourne - FIA Formula 2 Race 1 Report|date=2 April 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19095-r03-melbourne-fia-formula-2-race-1-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> However, in the feature race, Bearman's race came undone when he tangled with [[Isack Hadjar]] in the pits, sustaining a puncture. He had to pit again and had a trip to the gravel later on, finishing 17th.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2 April 2023 |title=Formula 2 - Leclerc takes first podium in Melbourne |url=https://www.ferrari.com/en-SG/fda/articles/formula-2-leclerc-takes-first-podium-in-melbourne |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230409051543/https://www.ferrari.com/en-SG/fda/articles/formula-2-leclerc-takes-first-podium-in-melbourne |archive-date=9 April 2023 |access-date=9 April 2023 |website=ferrari.com |language=en}}</ref> Bearman claimed his maiden pole position the next round in [[2023 Baku Formula 2 round|Baku]] in dramatic circumstances, managing to set the fastest lap despite a shunt just minutes before the end of the session which resulted in his steering wheel pointing slightly to the right.<ref>{{Cite web |date=28 April 2023 |title=QUALIFYING: Bearman snatches maiden pole in dramatic Baku ending |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/6vftrmETndKDFhXNpVZamS/qualifying-bearman-snatches-maiden-pole-in-dramatic-baku-ending |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230516182447/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/6vftrmETndKDFhXNpVZamS/qualifying-bearman-snatches-maiden-pole-in-dramatic-baku-ending |archive-date=16 May 2023 |access-date=16 May 2023 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Bearman grabs pole despite damage: 'Thanks to the team for making me stay out'|date=29 April 2023|url=https://feederseries.net/2023/04/29/bearman-grabs-pole-despite-damage-thanks-to-the-team-for-making-me-stay-out/|access-date=23 January 2025|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref> Starting the race ninth after a grid penalty for Pourchaire,<ref>{{Cite web |date=28 April 2023 |title=Théo Pourchaire handed post-Qualifying penalty |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5ub7WEDRikwgK7puJKzMbr/theo-pourchaire-handed-post-qualifying-penalty |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230501170449/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5ub7WEDRikwgK7puJKzMbr/theo-pourchaire-handed-post-qualifying-penalty |archive-date=1 May 2023 |access-date=16 May 2023 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref> Bearman came through the field to move up to fourth by lap 1. In the closing stages, leaders [[Dennis Hauger]], [[Victor Martins]] and [[Jehan Daruvala]] crashed out in turn 1 following a late safety car restart. After navigating around the pileup, Bearman capitalised on a mistake by teammate Vesti to take the lead before the race was neutralised once more, becoming the second youngest race winner in Formula 2.<ref>{{Cite web |date=29 April 2023 |title=SPRINT RACE: Bearman and PREMA prevail in Baku game of survival |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/66epuH0XPfyE81XN5xxGeH/sprint-race-bearman-and-prema-prevail-in-baku-game-of-survival |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230520164541/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/66epuH0XPfyE81XN5xxGeH/sprint-race-bearman-and-prema-prevail-in-baku-game-of-survival |archive-date=20 May 2023 |access-date=16 May 2023 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Alonso Lopez |first=Alejandro |date=30 April 2023 |title=Early move "crucial but not deciding" Baku F2 feature race win for Bearman |url=https://formulascout.com/early-move-crucial-but-not-deciding-baku-f2-feature-race-win-for-bearman/106361 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230516104503/https://formulascout.com/early-move-crucial-but-not-deciding-baku-f2-feature-race-win-for-bearman/106361 |archive-date=16 May 2023 |access-date=16 May 2023 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-GB}}</ref> The following day, the feature race, Bearman claimed victory and became the ninth driver in GP2 and Formula 2 history to do "the double" and only the fourth as a rookie.<ref>{{Cite web |date=30 April 2023 |title=FEATURE RACE: Bearman undefeated in Baku with back-to-back wins |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/schoJlFwLeaijmVFGGJXo/feature-race-bearman-undefeated-in-baku-with-back-to-back-wins |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230512150738/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/schoJlFwLeaijmVFGGJXo/feature-race-bearman-undefeated-in-baku-with-back-to-back-wins |archive-date=12 May 2023 |access-date=16 May 2023 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=4 May 2023 |title=How Ferrari junior Bearman blitzed the field in Baku to break F2 records |url=https://feederseries.net/2023/05/04/how-ferrari-junior-bearman-blitzed-the-field-in-baku-to-break-f2-records/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230516104503/https://feederseries.net/2023/05/04/how-ferrari-junior-bearman-blitzed-the-field-in-baku-to-break-f2-records/ |archive-date=16 May 2023 |access-date=16 May 2023 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref>

The next round in [[2023 Monte Carlo Formula 2 round|Monaco]] proved to be disappointing as Bearman retired on lap 23 of the sprint race due to a suspension problem;<ref>{{Cite web|title=R05 Monte Carlo - FIA Formula 2 Race 1 Report|date=28 May 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19129-r05-monte-carlo-fia-formula-2-race-1-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> in the feature race he finished just outside the points owing to a poor qualifying in 11th.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R05 Monte Carlo - FIA Formula 2 Race 2 Report|date=29 May 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19131-r05-monte-carlo-fia-formula-2-race-2-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Despite that, he retained his good form by scoring his second pole in [[2023 Barcelona Formula 2 round|Barcelona]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=QUALIFYING: Bearman leaves it late to secure second F2 pole position|date=2 June 2023|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/1jTjghdVjywtGwh2cliOZF/qualifying-bearman-leaves-it-late-to-secure-second-f2-pole-position|access-date=23 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Bearman hoping to banish 'a lot of inconsistency' at familiar European tracks|date=4 June 2023|url=https://feederseries.net/2023/06/04/bearman-hoping-to-banish-a-lot-of-inconsistency-at-familiar-european-tracks/|access-date=23 January 2025|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref> A good start in a wet sprint race meant Bearman finished in seventh place.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R06 Barcelona - FIA Formula 2 Race 1 Report|date=3 June 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19138-r06-barcelona-fia-formula-2-race-1-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> In the feature race, he fended off [[Enzo Fittipaldi]] at the start, and from there, he controlled the race to secure his third win.<ref>{{Cite web |title=FEATURE RACE: Bearman in control in Barcelona for third win of 2023 |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/7miXFHpBfQoLkEmBakYPjm/feature-race-bearman-in-control-in-barcelona-for-third-win-of-2023 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230622154252/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/7miXFHpBfQoLkEmBakYPjm/feature-race-bearman-in-control-in-barcelona-for-third-win-of-2023 |archive-date=22 June 2023 |access-date=16 June 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=5 June 2023|title=Bearman cites Drugovich's 2022 win as inspiring Barcelona strategy|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-cites-drugovichs-2022-win-as-inspiring-barcelona-strategy/107862|access-date=23 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> He qualified a disappointing 19th for the [[2023 Spielberg Formula 2 round|Austria]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=R07 Spielberg - FIA Formula 2 Qualifying Report|date=1 July 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19154-r07-spielberg-fia-formula-2-qualifying-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> In the sprint race, despite pitting for sluck tyres, Bearman was able to finish in eighth and score a point after a comeback.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R07 Spielberg - FIA Formula 2 Race 1 Report|date=2 July 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19157-r07-spielberg-fia-formula-2-race-1-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> A timely pit stop during the safety car allowed Bearman to make up a heap of places, and he eventually improved to fifth place after numerous overtakes on fresh tyres.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Oliver Bearman's Spielberg Weekend In His Words|date=4 July 2023|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/3UZg0gsJahjdANYl5oUFKc/oliver-bearmans-spielberg-weekend-in-his-words|access-date=23 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> In [[2023 Silverstone Formula 2 round|Silverstone]], Bearman qualified fifth and moved up to second briefly in the sprint. However, his race slowly unravelled as he spun, dropping him to sixth after a mistake into the gravel trap amidst a battle with [[Jack Doohan (racing driver)|Jack Doohan]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Bearman: Early confidence 'came back to bite us' after wet-to-dry Sprint Race struggles|date=8 July 2023|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5RI3ncJwKzBtKXOrqI2rWs/bearman-early-confidence-came-back-to-bite-us-after-wet-to-dry-sprint-race|access-date=23 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> A strong start saw him up to third, but contact later on with [[Kush Maini]] meant Bearman was given a five-second penalty, demoting him from sixth to eighth in the feature race.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Bearman and Nissany penalised after Silverstone Feature Race|date=9 July 2023|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/4gdhYxYbjXUJFMGJFEZnfZ/bearman-and-nissany-penalised-after-silverstone-feature-race|access-date=23 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref>

Bearman qualified seventh in [[2023 Budapest Formula 2 round|Hungary]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=R09 Hungaroring - FIA Formula 2 Qualifying Report|date=22 July 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19173-r09-hungaroring-fia-formula-2-qualifying-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Bearman finished in third place after a late lunge on Pourchaire in the dying laps meant he moved up to the rostrum places.<ref>{{Cite web|title=2023 Round 10 post-Sprint Race press conference|date=22 July 2023|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/2CgvojmI7Bxdh3XvhZdEuX/2023-round-10-post-sprint-race-press-conference|access-date=23 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> However, he lacked pace in the feature race, as he faded down to 13th place.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Formula 2: Bearman on the podium in Hungary|date=23 July 2023|url=https://www.ferrari.com/en-EN/fda/articles/formula-2-bearman-on-the-podium-in-hungary|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Scuderia Ferrari]]|language=en}}</ref> Bearman secure his third pole of the season in [[2023 Spa-Francorchamps Formula 2 round|Spa-Francorchamps]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=QUALIFYING: Bearman and PREMA beat the rain to secure Spa 1-2|date=28 July 2023|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/6FY1fwmANWHKYYEvSPJsQO/qualifying-bearman-and-prema-beat-the-rain-to-secure-spa-1-2|access-date=23 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=2023 Round 11 post-Qualifying press conference|date=28 July 2023|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/4ErA7NXIFyQBQ2yZoD15Tm/2023-round-11-post-qualifying-press-conference|access-date=23 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> In the feature race, he lost the lead in the pit stops to Pourchaire, and he eventually finished in fourth at the chequered flag, but contact with [[Victor Martins]] earned Bearman a penalty which dropped him to seventh place.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R10 Spa-Francorchamps - FIA Formula 2 Race 2 Report|date=31 July 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19186-r10-spa-francorchamps-fia-formula-2-race-2-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=30 July 2023|title=Prema's F2 front row pair explain where it went wrong on Sunday at Spa|url=https://formulascout.com/premas-f2-front-row-pair-explain-where-it-wrong-on-sunday-at-spa/109909|access-date=23 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> Starting sixth for the feature race in [[2023 Zandvoort Formula 2 round|Zandvoort]],<ref>{{Cite web|title=R11 Zandvoort - FIA Formula 2 Qualifying Report|date=25 August 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19193-r11-zandvoort-fia-formula-2-qualifying-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Bearman spun at the start after being hit by [[Juan Manuel Correa]] but he made his way back up the order, only for his race to end prematurely due to a collision with Martins, which broke Bearman's suspension.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R11 Zandvoort - FIA Formula 2 Race 2 Report|date=27 August 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19194-r11-zandvoort-fia-formula-2-race-2-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Bearman proceeded to qualify on the front row [[2023 Monza Formula 2 round|Monza]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=2023 Round 13 post-Qualifying press conference|date=1 September 2023|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5SdIRZxBqICeTo4oATfwBx/2023-round-13-post-qualifying-press-conference|access-date=23 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> Despite being shuffled outside the top 10 during the sprint race start, Bearman was able to gain place and finish in sixth position.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R12 Monza - FIA Formula 2 Race 1 Report|date=2 September 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19201-r12-monza-fia-formula-2-race-1-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> In the feature race, Bearman managed to pass polesitter Pourchaire at the start, and from there, he controlled the race for his fourth win,<ref>{{Cite web|title=FEATURE RACE: Bearman wins at Monza as Pourchaire extends title advantage|date=3 September 2023|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/1RZTdmreYk71jGL5DDsQl1/feature-race-bearman-wins-at-monza-as-pourchaire-extends-title-advantage|access-date=23 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Bearman: 'We've always been up there, but not quite finished up there' in rookie F2 season|date=3 September 2023|url=https://feederseries.net/2023/09/03/bearman-weve-always-been-up-there-but-not-quite-finished-up-there-in-rookie-f2-season/|access-date=23 January 2025|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref> placing him within one point of Martins for fifth in the standings.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Victor Martins vs Oliver Bearman: fighting for the second year running and top F2 rookie honours|date=15 November 2023|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/H2r0YmanzNvxwjXi7XUqv/victor-martins-vs-oliver-bearman-fighting-for-the-second-year-running-and|access-date=23 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref>

He qualified in a disappointing 17th for the [[2023 Yas Island Formula 2 round|Abu Dhabi season finale]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=R13 Abu Dhabi - FIA Formula 2 Qualifying Report|date=25 November 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19243-r13-abu-dhabi-fia-formula-2-qualifying-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> He finished the sprint in tenth,<ref>{{Cite web|title=R13 Abu Dhabi - FIA Formula 2 Race 1 Report|date=27 November 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19244-r13-abu-dhabi-fia-formula-2-race-1-report |access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> but an engine failure on lap 20 curtailed his race prematurely.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R13 Abu Dhabi - FIA Formula 2 Race 2 Report|date=27 November 2023|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19245-r13-abu-dhabi-fia-formula-2-race-2-report|access-date=23 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Despite this, Bearman ended his season sixth in the drivers' championship with 130 points, securing four wins, five podiums, two pole positions and two fastest laps. He also helped Prema secure second in the teams' championship.

==== 2024 ====
[[File:FIA F2 Austria 2024 Nr. 3 Bearman.jpg|thumb|Bearman driving for [[Prema Racing]] during the [[2024 Spielberg Formula 2 round]]]]
Bearman remained with [[Prema Racing]] for the [[2024 Formula 2 Championship|2024 season]], paired up with [[Mercedes Junior Team|Mercedes junior]] and [[2023 Formula Regional European Championship|2023 FRECA]] champion [[Andrea Kimi Antonelli]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=20 December 2023 |title=Oliver Bearman remains with PREMA Racing to complete 2024 lineup |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/2x0u36Gmno06xfqy30e2NQ/oliver-bearman-remains-with-prema-racing-to-complete-2024-lineup |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231220153652/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/2x0u36Gmno06xfqy30e2NQ/oliver-bearman-remains-with-prema-racing-to-complete-2024-lineup |archive-date=20 December 2023 |access-date=21 December 2023 |website=FIA F2 |language=en}}</ref> Prema struggled to adapt to the [[Dallara F2 2024|new regulations]] at the start of the season,<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/f1-hopefuls-antonelli-and-bearman-struggle-to-shine-in-new-look-f2-spanish-gp-diary/ |title=F1 hopefuls Antonelli and Bearman struggle to shine in new-look F2: Spanish GP diary |last=Medland |first=Chris |date=24 June 2024 |magazine=[[Motor Sport (magazine)|Motor Sport]] |access-date=24 January 2025 |issn=0027-2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241209213220/https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/f1-hopefuls-antonelli-and-bearman-struggle-to-shine-in-new-look-f2-spanish-gp-diary/ |archive-date=9 December 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/single-seater-open-wheel/five-things-learned-puzzlingly-wild-f2-season-so-far/ |title=Five things we've learned from a puzzlingly wild F2 season so far |last=Kanal |first=Samarth |date=21 August 2024 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=24 January 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241209182936/https://www.the-race.com/single-seater-open-wheel/five-things-learned-puzzlingly-wild-f2-season-so-far/ |archive-date=9 December 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> as Bearman came away without points in the [[2024 Sakhir Formula 2 round|Bahrain opener]] owing to qualifying down in 18th.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Gascoigne|first=Roger|date=4 March 2024|title=How Bearman's "biggest year" made a stuttering start in Bahrain|url=https://formulascout.com/how-bearmans-biggest-year-made-a-stuttering-start-in-bahrain/116312|access-date=24 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> Despite his struggles, Bearman qualified on pole for the next round in [[2024 Jeddah Formula 2 round|Jeddah]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=QUALIFYING: Bearman beats Maini to Jeddah pole|date=7 March 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5g7ovxgbXCj4ijmhtRt9pA/qualifying-bearman-beats-maini-to-jeddah-pole|access-date=24 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Bearman: 'No doubt we can be strong' after taking Jeddah pole|date=7 March 2024|url=https://feederseries.net/2024/03/07/bearman-no-doubt-we-can-be-strong-after-taking-jeddah-pole/|access-date=24 January 2025|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref> However, he withdrew from the event to replace [[Carlos Sainz Jr|Carlos Sainz]] at [[Scuderia Ferrari|Ferrari]] for the {{F1GP|2024|Saudi Arabian}}.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Oliver Bearman to make F1 debut replacing Carlos Sainz in Saudi Arabian Grand Prix|date=8 March 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/YZGpGfsSqYqjeaFnhG3LK/oliver-bearman-to-make-f1-debut-replacing-carlos-sainz-in-saudi-arabian|access-date=24 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> Bearman returned in [[2024 Melbourne Formula 2 round|Melbourne]], but a technical issue in qualifying limited him to only 16th.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=22 March 2024|title=Antonelli jubilant with his F2 qualifying as Bearman rues technical issue|url=https://formulascout.com/antonelli-jubilant-with-his-f2-qualifying-as-bearman-rues-technical-issue/117060|access-date=24 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> He was set to score his first points in the sprint race with eighth,<ref>{{Cite web|title=R03 Melbourne - FIA Formula 2 Race 1 Report|date=23 March 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19280-r03-melbourne-fia-formula-2-race-1-report|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> but received a penalty for forcing [[Joshua Dürksen]] wide, dropping him to 14th.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Isack Hadjar loses Sprint Race win, Bearman and Crawford also penalised|date=23 March 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/4BmF0R0l1XqWdKfUPy0Ycg/isack-hadjar-loses-sprint-race-win-bearman-and-crawford-penalised|access-date=24 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> In the feature race, despite being held in a double stack pit stop under the [[safety car]], Bearman finished ninth, scoring his first points.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R03 Melbourne - FIA Formula 2 Race 2 Report|date=24 March 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19283-r03-melbourne-fia-formula-2-race-2-report|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Bearman then qualified second at [[2024 Imola Formula 2 round|Imola]],<ref>{{Cite web|title=Round 4 Post Qualifying Press Conference|date=17 May 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/1h9yGf2moW53Q3RYI9TRHs/round-4-post-qualifying-press-conference|access-date=24 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> finishing the sprint in fifth place as he took advantage of a first lap multi-car accident to move up the order.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R04 Imola - FIA Formula 2 Race 1 Report|date=18 May 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19296-r04-imola-fia-formula-2-race-1-report|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> During the feature race, Bearman took the lead on the opening lap but stalled during his mandatory pit stop, condemning him to 19th at the chequered flag.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R04 Imola - FIA Formula 2 Race 2 Report|date=19 May 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19298-r04-imola-fia-formula-2-race-2-report|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref>

Bearman qualified 15th in [[2024 Monte Carlo Formula 2 round|Monte Carlo]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=R05 Monte Carlo - FIA Formula 2 Qualifying Report|date=24 May 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19303-r05-monte-carlo-fia-formula-2-qualifying-report|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> In the feature race, a bold strategy call for an early stop meant Bearman finished fourth, his best finish of the season at that point.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Bearman says he has 'high hopes' for the rest of the season after P4 in Monte Carlo|date=31 May 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5UG2B9wLlKzIeCLUEr9Y9n/bearman-says-he-has-high-hopes-for-the-rest-of-the-season-after-p4-in-monte|access-date=24 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> A torrid weekend followed in [[2024 Barcelona Formula 2 round|Barcelona]], where finished the sprint 21st due to track limits penalties,<ref>{{Cite web|title=R06 Barcelona - FIA Formula 2 Race 1 Report|date=22 June 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19321-r06-barcelona-fia-formula-2-race-1-report|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> and finished the feature race 14th, where Valentin Khorounzhiy of ''The Race'' described his weekend as "truly turgid, amid balance struggles manifesting what the team described as ''strong understeer'' - which then also seemingly translated into the tyres getting absolutely shredded over longer runs".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/ollie-bearman-f2-season-bad-enough-for-f1-haas-to-care/|title=Is Bearman's F2 season bad enough for F1 to care?|date=25 June 2024|access-date=28 November 2024|website=The Race|first=Valentin|last=Khorounzhiy}}</ref> Bearman finally broke his duck in [[2024 Spielberg Formula 2 round|Austria]] by winning the sprint race from second, where he held off [[Pepe Martí]] for his first victory.<ref>{{Cite web|title=SPRINT RACE: Bearman holds off Martí to take victory in Spielberg|date=29 June 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/7nS3fSSRJLuCY1swZYFBSw/sprint-race-bearman-holds-off-marti-to-take-victory-in-spielberg|access-date=24 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Alonso Lopez|first=Alejandro|date=29 June 2024|title=Bearman happy to pay back Prema's hard work with first F2 win of 2024|url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-happy-to-pay-back-premas-hard-work-with-first-f2-win-of-2024/120722|access-date=24 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> Speaking about his win, Bearman admitted it was "painful" to not be fighting for the championship.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://feederseries.net/2024/06/29/bearman-painful-to-be-out-of-f2-championship-fight/|title=Bearman: 'Painful' to be out of F2 championship fight|website=Feeder Series|date=29 June 2024|access-date=28 November 2024|first=Steven|last=Walton}}</ref> His feature race however, was a complete contrast, as he retired on lap 21 with an engine issue.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R07 Spielberg - FIA Formula 2 Race 2 Report|date=30 June 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19330-r07-spielberg-fia-formula-2-race-2-report|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Bearman qualified fifth for [[2024 Silverstone Formula 2 round|Silverstone]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Bearman feeling home race love after promising P5 in Silverstone Qualifying|date=5 July 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/67DpJcPWKtfo4to3TaUqkR/bearman-feeling-home-race-love-after-promising-p5-in-silverstone-qualifying|access-date=24 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> In the sprint race, he damaged his front wing on the opening lap following contact with [[Gabriel Bortoleto]], before retiring on lap 15 from another engine issue.<ref name="premaracing.com">{{Cite web|title=R08 Silverstone - FIA Formula 2 Race 1 Report|date=6 July 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19336-r08-silverstone-fia-formula-2-race-1-report|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> In the feature race, he briefly moved to second after a good start, but eventually fell to seventh.<ref name="premaracing.com"/>

Bearman failed to score points in [[2024 Budapest Formula 2 round|Hungary]] once again after a poor qualifying.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Formula 2: Qualifying complicates Bearman's weekend|date=23 July 2024|url=https://www.ferrari.com/en-EN/fda/articles/formula-2-qualifying-complicates-bearmans-weekend|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Scuderia Ferrari]]|language=en}}</ref>
More woes followed for Bearman in [[2024 Spa-Francorchamps Formula 2 round|Spa-Francorchamps]], as during the feature race, Bearman crashed out on the opening lap after a collision with [[Zane Maloney]] and Martí, and he was given a five-place grid drop for the next round.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R10 Spa-Francorchamps - FIA Formula 2 Race 2 Report|date=29 July 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19362-r10-spa-francorchamps-fia-formula-2-race-2-report|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=28 July 2024|title=Prema drivers handed grid penalties for next F2 round|url=https://formulascout.com/prema-drivers-handed-grid-penalties-for-next-f2-round/122205|access-date=24 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> In [[2024 Monza Formula 2 round|Monza]], Bearman won the sprint race from eighth on the grid as he slowly made his way up the order for a second triumph.<ref>{{Cite web|title=SPRINT RACE: Bearman dominates to take victory in entertaining Monza battle|date=31 August 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5kIbLWZBIQ3ztEPtz0iKuN/sprint-race-bearman-dominates-to-take-victory-in-entertaining-monza-battle|access-date=24 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Round 11 Post Sprint Race Press Conference|date=31 August 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5VigsKqJj2jILlIYyIedhb/round-11-post-sprint-race-press-conference|access-date=24 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> After improving to second at the start of the feature race, he duelled with teammate Antonelli and eventually finished seventh, his first double points finish of the season.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R11 Monza - FIA Formula 2 Race 2 Report|date=1 September 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19376-r11-monza-fia-formula-2-race-2-report|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Bearman missed the next round in [[2024 Baku Formula 2 round|Baku]] to replace a banned [[Kevin Magnussen]] at [[Haas F1 Team|Haas]] for the {{F1GP|2024|Azerbaijan}}.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Oliver Bearman confirmed to replace Kevin Magnussen for Azerbaijan Grand Prix|date=6 September 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5IBAYesypvQDLnmvpnyuFx/oliver-bearman-confirmed-to-replace-kevin-magnussen-for-azerbaijan-grand|access-date=24 January 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref>

Bearman qualified on reverse pole in [[2024 Lusail Formula 2 round|Qatar]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/4lfOijVmFbFlKhaCMbH1Y3/qualifying-aron-unbeatable-in-lusail|title=QUALIFYING: Aron unbeatable in Lusail|date=29 November 2024|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=R13 Qatar - FIA Formula 2 Qualifying Report|date=29 November 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19421-r13-qatar-fia-formula-2-qualifying-report|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Despite being passed by [[Isack Hadjar]] early in the sprint race, Bearman eventually re-passed him to secure his third win of the year.<ref>{{Cite web |date=30 November 2024 |title=SPRINT: Bearman wins in Lusail with late-race pass on Hadjar|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/4k0yl7ZREjq8IDO0fVqsHk/sprint-bearman-wins-in-lusail-with-late-race-pass-on-hadjar|access-date=7 December 2024 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Alonso Lopez|first=Alejandro|date=1 December 2024|title='Patience' rewarded both Bearman and Crawford in Qatar F2 sprint race|url=https://formulascout.com/patience-rewarded-both-bearman-and-crawford-in-qatar-f2-sprint-race/126140|access-date=24 January 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> The feature race did not go as planned as an early safety car dashed Bearman's hopes on the alternate strategy, and he eventually placed down in 12th place.<ref>{{Cite web |date=1 December 2024 |title=FEATURE RACE: Aron claims first Formula 2 victory in action-packed Lusail affair|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/7Gn9X00LeSGXlBBIfhuPWr/feature-race-feature-race-aron-claims-first-formula-2-victory-in-action|access-date=7 December 2024 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=R13 Qatar - FIA Formula 2 Race 2 Report|date=1 December 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19423-r13-qatar-fia-formula-2-race-2-report|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> He qualified 15th for the season finale in [[2024 Yas Island Formula 2 round|Abu Dhabi]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=R14 Abu Dhabi - FIA Formula 2 Qualifying Report|date=6 December 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19428-r14-abu-dhabi-fia-formula-2-qualifying-report|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Bearman made good comebacks during the races, finishing in fourth during the sprint and fifth in the feature.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Formula 2: Dino on the podium, Ollie comes close|date=18 December 2024|url=https://www.ferrari.com/en-EN/fda/articles/formula-2-dino-on-the-podium-ollie-comes-close|access-date=24 January 2025|website=[[Scuderia Ferrari]]|language=en}}</ref> Bearman finished his season a disappointing 12th in the driver's standings with 75 points despite being considered as a title favourite going into the season. On his season, Bearman said, "It was tough to not be fighting for wins regularly, but I will have seasons like this in my career and it has been a great learning experience." During the season, he took three wins and one fastest lap.

== Formula One career ==
[[File:Goodwood edited-075 (53863491669).jpg|thumb|left|Bearman demonstrating the [[Ferrari SF71H]] at the [[Goodwood Festival of Speed]] in 2024]]
In October 2021, Bearman was named as one of the finalists of the [[Ferrari Driver Academy]]'s Scouting World Final.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=12 October 2021 |title=Italian F4 champion Bearman makes final of Ferrari Scouting World Final |url=https://formulascout.com/italian-f4-champion-bearman-makes-final-of-ferrari-scouting-world-final/85155 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211012165316/https://formulascout.com/italian-f4-champion-bearman-makes-final-of-ferrari-scouting-world-final/85155 |archive-date=12 October 2021 |access-date=7 November 2021 |website=Formula Scout}}</ref> The following month, Bearman was confirmed to be joining the academy along with karting champion [[Rafael Câmara]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=8 November 2021 |title=British youngster Bearman joins Ferrari Driver Academy |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/british-youngster-bearman-joins-ferrari-driver-academy/6759344/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211108113520/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/british-youngster-bearman-joins-ferrari-driver-academy/6759344/ |archive-date=8 November 2021 |access-date=8 November 2021 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]]}}</ref>

In October 2023, Bearman made his first test in a [[Formula One car]] during a private session at [[Fiorano Circuit|Fiorano]] with Ferrari.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=11 October 2023 |title=Bearman does first F1 test with Ferrari at Fiorano |url=https://formulascout.com/bearman-does-first-f1-test-with-ferrari-at-fiorano/112003 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231012024634/https://formulascout.com/bearman-does-first-f1-test-with-ferrari-at-fiorano/112003 |archive-date=12 October 2023 |access-date=12 October 2023 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-GB}}</ref> He made his [[Formula One racing#Free practice|free practice]] debut at the [[2023 Mexico City Grand Prix]] with [[Haas F1 Team]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Noble |first=Jonathan |date=5 October 2023 |title=Ferrari junior Bearman to get Haas FP1 outings in Mexico and Abu Dhabi |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/bearman-to-get-haas-fp1-outings-in-mexico-and-abu-dhabi/10528804/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231005121249/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/bearman-to-get-haas-fp1-outings-in-mexico-and-abu-dhabi/10528804/ |archive-date=5 October 2023 |access-date=5 October 2023 |website=[[Motorsport.com]]}}</ref> He finished 15th, and was only three tenths off Haas driver [[Nico Hülkenberg]]. Haas stated they were "very impressed" with his performance.<ref>{{Cite web |date=28 October 2023 |title=Friday at the Mexico City Grand Prix |url=https://www.haasf1team.com/news/friday-mexico-city-grand-prix |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231107130004/https://www.haasf1team.com/news/friday-mexico-city-grand-prix |archive-date=7 November 2023 |access-date=7 November 2023 |website=[[Haas F1 Team]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Cooper |first=Adam |date=29 October 2023 |title=Haas "very impressed" by Bearman after Mexico GP FP1 rookie run |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/haas-impressed-by-bearman-after-mexico-gp-fp1-rookie-run/10538893/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231107130001/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/haas-impressed-by-bearman-after-mexico-gp-fp1-rookie-run/10538893/ |archive-date=7 November 2023 |access-date=7 November 2023 |website=[[Motorsport.com]]}}</ref> He took part in his second free practice at the {{F1GP|2023|Abu Dhabi}}.<ref>{{Cite web |date=24 November 2023 |title=Abu Dhabi Grand Prix: Friday Practice Recap |url=https://www.haasf1team.com/news/abu-dhabi-grand-prix-friday-practice-recap-1 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231221081336/https://www.haasf1team.com/news/abu-dhabi-grand-prix-friday-practice-recap-1 |archive-date=21 December 2023 |access-date=21 December 2023 |website=[[Haas F1 Team]] |language=en}}</ref> Bearman then drove the [[Haas VF-23|VF-23]] in the young drivers' test.<ref>{{Cite web |date=21 November 2023 |title=Bearman and Fittipaldi to drive for Haas in post-season Abu Dhabi test |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.bearman-and-fittipaldi-to-drive-for-haas-in-post-season-abu-dhabi-test.1CTsOwtNlhWb3tYAlcF4f0.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231121145827/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.bearman-and-fittipaldi-to-drive-for-haas-in-post-season-abu-dhabi-test.1CTsOwtNlhWb3tYAlcF4f0.html |archive-date=21 November 2023 |access-date=21 November 2023 |website=[[Formula 1]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=28 November 2023 |title=Ocon sets the pace as Russell car failure causes heavy crash in post-season Abu Dhabi test |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.esteban-ocon-george-russell-post-season-abu-dhabi-test.7eLZKeQzlNqFZBvQ5O6WcP.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231215075748/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.esteban-ocon-george-russell-post-season-abu-dhabi-test.7eLZKeQzlNqFZBvQ5O6WcP.html |archive-date=15 December 2023 |access-date=21 December 2023 |website=[[Formula 1]] |language=en}}</ref>

On 27 January 2024, Bearman was announced as Ferrari's reserve driver for the {{F1|2024}} season, sharing the role with [[Robert Shwartzman]] and [[Antonio Giovinazzi]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Cooper |first=Adam |date=27 January 2024 |title=Ferrari adds Bearman to F1 reserve roster for 2024 |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ferrari-adds-bearman-to-f1-reserve-roster-for-2024/10569708/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240128043535/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/ferrari-adds-bearman-to-f1-reserve-roster-for-2024/10569708/ |archive-date=28 January 2024 |access-date=28 January 2024 |website=[[Motorsport.com]]}}</ref> He was also later confirmed as a reserve driver for Haas,<ref>{{Cite web |date=1 February 2024 |title=Oliver Bearman and Pietro Fittipaldi Named Official Reserve Drivers for MoneyGram Haas F1 Team |url=https://www.haasf1team.com/news/oliver-bearman-and-pietro-fittipaldi-named-official-reserve-drivers-moneygram-haas-f1-team |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240201102843/https://www.haasf1team.com/news/oliver-bearman-and-pietro-fittipaldi-named-official-reserve-drivers-moneygram-haas-f1-team |archive-date=1 February 2024 |access-date=1 February 2024 |website=[[Haas F1 Team]] |language=en}}</ref> and drove the [[Haas VF-24]] during first practice at the {{F1GP|2024|Emilia Romagna}} in place of [[Kevin Magnussen]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/2gtoB2Y0qQ4m2YYa3gTVzE/oliver-bearman-set-for-fp1-sessions-and-reserve-driver-role-with-haas|title=Oliver Bearman set for FP1 sessions and Reserve Driver role with Haas|publisher=Formula 2|date=1 February 2024|access-date=12 May 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Smith |first1=Luke |title=Magnussen's tactics have helped Haas — and put him in danger of a race ban |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5484738/2024/05/13/kevin-magnussen-f1-penalty-points-race-ban/ |access-date=14 May 2024 |work=The New York Times |date=13 May 2024|quote= Bearman will take part in FP1 for Haas at Imola next weekend, his first of six scheduled practice appearances with the team over the course of the season.}}</ref> He drove the VF-24 again during the [[Pirelli]] tyre test at [[Silverstone Circuit|Silverstone]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Bearman and Fittipaldi to drive for Haas in Pirelli F1 tyre test|date=6 July 2024|url=https://www.motorsportweek.com/2024/07/06/bearman-and-fittipaldi-to-drive-for-haas-in-pirelli-f1-tyre-test/|access-date=13 July 2024|website=Motorsport Week|language=en}}</ref> Bearman drove the [[Ferrari SF-24]] during first practice at the {{F1GP|2024|Mexico City}}, but his running ended prematurely following a collision with [[Alex Albon]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Marino |first=Alex |date=18 October 2024 |title=Oliver Bearman returns in Ferrari SF-24: he will drive in Mexico FP1 |url=https://scuderiafans.com/oliver-bearman-returns-in-ferrari-sf-24-he-will-drive-in-mexico-fp1/ |access-date=26 October 2024 |website=Scuderia Fans |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=25 October 2024 |title=Albon and Bearman collide in opening F1 Mexican GP practice |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/alex-albon-ollie-bearman-crash-f1-mexican-practice-one/ |access-date=26 October 2024 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref>

=== Ferrari/Haas reserve driver (2024) ===
Bearman made his Formula One debut at the [[2024 Saudi Arabian Grand Prix]], replacing [[Carlos Sainz Jr.]] after he withdrew from the event with [[appendicitis]] following the second free practice session,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lloyd |first=Martin |date=8 March 2024 |title=How F2's Ollie Bearman reached Formula 1 |url=https://feederseries.net/2024/03/08/how-f2s-ollie-bearman-reached-formula-1/ |access-date=8 March 2024 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref> becoming the youngest-ever driver to compete for [[Scuderia Ferrari|Ferrari]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=8 March 2024 |title=Bearman replaces Sainz at Ferrari for Saudi Arabian GP after appendicitis diagnosis |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/bearman-replaces-sainz-for-saudi-arabian-grand-prix/10584719/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240308130812/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/bearman-replaces-sainz-for-saudi-arabian-grand-prix/10584719/ |archive-date=8 March 2024 |access-date=8 March 2024 |website=Autosport}}</ref> Bearman qualified eleventh, missing out on Q3 by 36 hundredths.<ref>{{Cite web |title="Bin wirklich beeindruckt": Selbst Hamilton staunt über Bearman-Debüt |url=https://www.formel1.de/news/grand-prix-berichte/2024-03-08/bin-wirklich-beeindruckt-selbst-hamilton-staunt-ueber-bearman-debuet |access-date=9 March 2024 |website=Formel1.de |language=de}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Ferrari super-sub Bearman says missing Q3 in quali debut 'hurts' as Leclerc looks to 'surprise' Red Bulls in Saudi|date=8 March 2024|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/ferrari-super-sub-bearman-says-missing-q3-in-quali-debut-hurts-as-leclerc.29XNHGiH4R3FaZfA1D2rHe|access-date=25 January 2025|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en}}</ref> In the race, Bearman was able to hold off [[Lando Norris]] and [[Lewis Hamilton]] in the closing stages of the race to secure seventh place and his maiden points finish;<ref>{{Cite web|title=Bearman 'destroyed' after points-scoring Ferrari debut as he reflects on 'good showing' in Saudi Arabia|date=9 March 2024|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/bearman-destroyed-after-points-scoring-ferrari-debut-as-he-reflects-on-good.6cKjZbfNRJkPZBjW0KqiED|access-date=25 January 2025|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en}}</ref> he became the [[List of Formula One driver records#Youngest drivers to start a race|then-youngest driver to score points on debut]] in Formula One.<ref>{{Cite web|title=How Bearman's F1 debut provided a refreshing feel-good story|date=11 March 2024|url=https://www.motorsportweek.com/2024/03/11/how-bearmans-f1-debut-provided-a-refreshing-feel-good-story/|access-date=25 January 2025|website=Motorsport Week|language=en}}</ref> Additionally, he was voted ''Driver of the Day'' by the fans and received widespread acclaim from drivers and critics for his performance on short notice.<ref>{{Cite web |date=9 March 2024 |title=DRIVER OF THE DAY: Bearman wins by a landslide with P7 on debut for Ferrari in Jeddah |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.driver-of-the-day-bearman-wins-by-a-landslide-with-p7-on-debut-for-ferrari.52dNKTOa7s1vy4MFmOzTVA.html |access-date=9 March 2024}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=8 March 2024 |title=Hamilton praises Bearman's F1 debut: 'No way I was ready at 18' |url=https://www.motorsportweek.com/2024/03/08/hamilton-praises-bearmans-f1-debut-no-way-i-was-ready-at-18/ |access-date=9 March 2024 |website=Motorsport Week}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.facts-and-stats-bearman-makes-it-four-brits-in-the-points-for-the-first-time.7lmU47WyQN1CvdbdY5TxD0.html|title=Best facts and stats after the Grand Prix in Saudi Arabia|website=www.formula1.com|access-date=11 March 2024}}</ref> Teammate [[Charles Leclerc]] also stated that it was "a matter of time before we see [him] permanently in the Formula 1 paddock".<ref>{{Cite web|title=Leclerc says 'it's a matter of time' before Bearman joins F1 grid after Saudi stand-in performance|date=10 March 2024|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/leclerc-says-its-a-matter-of-time-before-bearman-joins-f1-grid-after-saudi.2AKJR26mdQUU1HGphDOAbt|access-date=25 January 2025|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en}}</ref> Bearman was put on standby for the {{F1 GP|2024|Australian}}, but ultimately Sainz was fit enough to drive.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ferrari provide update on Sainz ahead of Australian Grand Prix with reserve driver Bearman on call in Melbourne|date=20 March 2024|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/ferrari-provide-update-on-sainz-ahead-of-australian-grand-prix-with-reserve.5KF1LNxx4DDBgDCzdBVFZu|access-date=25 January 2025|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en}}</ref>

Between Saudi Arabia and Azerbaijan, Bearman took part in four practice sessions for Haas as a young/reserve driver.

In July, [[Haas F1 Team|Haas]] announced that Bearman had signed a multi-year contract with the team from {{F1|2025}} onwards, following months of speculation.<ref name="contract">{{Cite news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5614599/2024/07/04/oliver-bearman-haas-f1/ |title=Oliver Bearman announced as Haas F1 driver for 2025 season |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=4 July 2024 |work=[[The Athletic]] |publisher=[[The New York Times]] |access-date=18 March 2025 |issn=1553-8095 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240916192614/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5614599/2024/07/04/oliver-bearman-haas-f1/ |archive-date=16 September 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Lloyd |first=Martin |date=4 July 2024 |title=Ferrari junior Bearman earns 2025 Haas F1 race seat |url=https://feederseries.net/2024/07/04/ferrari-junior-bearman-earns-2025-haas-f1-race-seat/ |access-date=4 July 2024 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref> Bearman made an early debut for Haas at the {{F1GP|2024|Azerbaijan}}, after [[Kevin Magnussen]] received a race ban.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/bearman-to-replace-banned-magnussen-at-haas-for-azerbaijan-grand.AkCoDVRDHBHPpNdlyqMzv|title=Bearman to replace banned Magnussen at Haas for Azerbaijan Grand Prix|website=Formula 1.com|date=6 September 2024|access-date=6 September 2024}}</ref> He narrowly missed out on a Q3 appearance once again, as he qualified eleventh but ahead of teammate [[Nico Hülkenberg]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Cleeren|first=Filip|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/bearman-disappointed-at-baku-q3-miss-despite-outqualifying-hulkenberg/10654218/|date=14 September 2024|title=Bearman disappointed at Baku Q3 miss despite outqualifying Hulkenberg|access-date=25 January 2025|website=[[Motorsport.com]]}}</ref> In the race, Bearman finished tenth, beating Hülkenberg in both sessions to score another points finish and become the first driver in history to score points for two different teams in his first two races.<ref>{{Cite web|title='It's my fault' – Bearman reflects on 'not fully deserved' point in Baku despite making history|date=16 September 2024|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/its-my-fault-bearman-reflects-on-not-fully-deserved-point-in-baku-despite.MSVNYn1ZvBl4lpyFxL6td|access-date=25 January 2025|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en}}</ref> Bearman again deputised for Magnussen at the {{F1GP|2024|São Paulo}}, after Magnussen withdrew due to illness.<ref>{{Cite web |date=1 November 2024 |title=Magnussen out for Brazilian GP, Bearman gets full race weekend |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/magnussen-out-for-brazilian-gp-bearman-gets-full-race-weekend/10669382/ |access-date=1 November 2024 |website=Autosport |language=en |quote="Haas F1 Team can confirm that Kevin Magnussen will not compete in the São Paulo Grand Prix and Oliver Bearman will race for the team for the remainder of the weekend," the team shared in a statement, with Autosport understanding Magnussen's symptoms are nausea-related.}}</ref> He beat Hülkenberg in both sprint sessions, where he qualified tenth and finished fourteenth.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Bearman thrilled to reach SQ3 in Sao Paulo amid last-minute Haas call-up as several surprise names make top 10|date=1 November 2024|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/bearman-thrilled-to-reach-sq3-in-sao-paulo-amid-last-minute-haas-call-up-as.7E6m4JHmLTKsLSpsLBwY6y|access-date=25 January 2025|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=São Paulo Grand Prix: Sprint Race / Qualifying Recap|date=2 November 2024|url=https://www.haasf1team.com/news/sao-paulo-grand-prix-sprint-race-qualifying-recap|access-date=25 January 2025|website=[[Haas F1 Team]]|language=en}}</ref> Bearman was involved in several incidents in the wet-weather conditions during the Grand Prix—including a 10-second time penalty for causing a collision with [[Franco Colapinto]] and a high speed spin, he qualified sixteenth and finished twelfth.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Bearman pleased with learning opportunities from Sao Paulo |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/too-many-mistakes-too-many-time-losses-bearman-gives-brutal-verdict-on-his.32GIYdxfaQI1VJcsBxMv86 |access-date=15 November 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref>

=== Haas (2025–present) ===
[[File:2025 Japan GP - Haas - Oliver Bearman - FP2.jpg|thumb|Bearman (pictured at the {{F1GP|2025|Japanese}}) signed for [[Haas F1 Team|Haas]] as a full-time driver in {{F1|2025}}.|alt=Bearman driving the Haas VF-25 at the 2025 Japanese Grand Prix|left]]

==== 2025: Rookie season ====
Bearman was partnered with former [[Alpine F1 Team|Alpine]] driver [[Esteban Ocon]] for {{F1|2025}}.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cv2gzp0v0z7o |title=Haas sign Alpine's Ocon for 2025 season |date=25 July 2024 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=22 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240829182841/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cv2gzp0v0z7o |archive-date=29 August 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> At the season-opening {{F1GP|2025|Australian}}, he crashed out of both [[free practice]] sessions he entered—missing the second session due to collision damage—and was unable to qualify after a [[gearbox]] issue;<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/rookies-face-brutal-f1-reality-the-heroes-and-zeroes-heading-into-wet-australian-gp/ |url-access=registration |title=Brutal F1 reality for rookies: qualifying bites hard ahead of wet Australian GP |last=Cooper |first=Adam |date=15 March 2025 |magazine=[[Motor Sport (magazine)|Motor Sport]] |access-date=15 March 2025 |issn=0027-2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250315182951/https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/rookies-face-brutal-f1-reality-the-heroes-and-zeroes-heading-into-wet-australian-gp/ |archive-date=15 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> after being permitted to start by the [[FIA]], he placed last of the finishers in fourteenth.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.roadandtrack.com/news/a64242735/formula-1-2025-rookies-set-up-to-fail/ |title=All 6 of Formula 1's 2025 Rookies Have Been Set Up to Fail |last=Smith |first=Fred |date=20 March 2025 |magazine=[[Road & Track]] |publisher=[[Hearst Magazines]] |access-date=22 March 2025 |issn=0035-7189 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250322234225/https://www.roadandtrack.com/news/a64242735/formula-1-2025-rookies-set-up-to-fail/ |archive-date=22 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He finished eighth at the {{F1GP|2025|Chinese}} after disqualifications for both [[Scuderia Ferrari|Ferrari]] drivers, achieving his first [[List of Formula One points scoring systems|points finish]] in the [[Haas VF-25|VF-25]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/leclerc-hamilton-and-gasly-disqualified-from-chinese-gp/10706422/ |title=Leclerc, Hamilton and Gasly disqualified from Chinese GP |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=23 March 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=23 March 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250323122436/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/leclerc-hamilton-and-gasly-disqualified-from-chinese-gp/10706422/ |archive-date=23 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He scored further points with tenth-placed finishes in [[2025 Japanese Grand Prix|Japan]] and [[2025 Bahrain Grand Prix|Bahrain]], having qualified last at the latter.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-a-trio-of-rookies-impressed-at-the-f1-japanese-gp/10710552/ |title=How a trio of rookies impressed at the F1 Japanese GP |last=Mann-Bryans |first=Mark |date=6 April 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=6 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250406175608/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-a-trio-of-rookies-impressed-at-the-f1-japanese-gp/10710552/ |archive-date=6 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/how-bearman-went-from-last-to-the-points-in-bahrain-gp/ |url-access=registration |title=How Bearman went from last to the points in Bahrain GP |last=Elizalde |first=Pablo |date=14 April 2025 |magazine=[[Motor Sport (magazine)|Motor Sport]] |access-date=15 April 2025 |issn=0027-2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250415161810/https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/how-bearman-went-from-last-to-the-points-in-bahrain-gp/ |archive-date=15 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He claimed thirteenth at the {{F1GP|2025|Saudi Arabian}}.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.autoweek.com/racing/formula-1/a64533955/first-turn-decides-oscar-piastri-cruises-f1-saudi-arabian-gp-win/ |title=First Turn Decides It as Oscar Piastri Cruises to F1 Saudi Arabian GP Win |last=Horton |first=Phillip |date=20 April 2025 |magazine=[[Autoweek]] |publisher=[[Hearst Communications]] |access-date=21 April 2025 |issn=0192-9674 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250421215406/https://www.autoweek.com/racing/formula-1/a64533955/first-turn-decides-oscar-piastri-cruises-f1-saudi-arabian-gp-win/ |archive-date=21 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He climbed from nineteenth to eighth in the rain-affected {{F1GP|2025|Miami}} sprint, demoted to fourteenth following a penalty for an unsafe [[pit stop|pit]] release;<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/penalty-costs-bearman-miami-points-finish/ |title=Penalties cost three drivers Miami sprint points finishes |last=Benyon |first=Jack |date=3 May 2025|website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=3 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250503203424/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/penalty-costs-bearman-miami-points-finish/ |archive-date=3 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> he suffered an engine failure whilst running in twelfth in the main race.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.autohebdo.fr/breves/f1/bearman-et-bortoleto-abandonnent-le-gp-de-miami-sur-problemes-moteurs.html |title=Bearman et Bortoleto abandonnent le GP de Miami sur problèmes moteurs |trans-title=Bearman and Bortoleto abandon the Miami GP due to engine problems |last=Chambenoit |first=Mathieu |date=4 May 2025 |magazine=Auto Hebdo |language=fr |issn=0395-4366 |access-date=5 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250805122950/https://www.autohebdo.fr/breves/f1/bearman-et-bortoleto-abandonnent-le-gp-de-miami-sur-problemes-moteurs.html |archive-date=5 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He finished seventeenth in [[2025 Emilia Romagna Grand Prix|Emilia Romagna]], twelfth in [[2025 Monaco Grand Prix|Monaco]], and seventeenth again in [[2025 Spanish Grand Prix|Spain]]; he narrowly missed out on setting a qualifying lap at the former,<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/f1-2025-imola-grand-prix-driver-rankings/ |title=Edd Straw's 2025 F1 Imola Grand Prix driver rankings |last=Straw |first=Edd |date=19 May 2025 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=5 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250623001245/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/f1-2025-imola-grand-prix-driver-rankings/ |archive-date=23 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> was penalised for a [[red flag (motorsport)|red flag]] infringement in Monaco,<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/bearman-suffers-10-place-grid-penalty-for-f1-monaco-gp/10725768/ |title=Bearman suffers 10-place grid penalty for F1 Monaco GP |last=Selleck |first=Emily |date=23 May 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=5 August 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250523214858/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/bearman-suffers-10-place-grid-penalty-for-f1-monaco-gp/10725768/ |archive-date=23 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-monaco-gp-report/10726566/ |title=F1 Monaco GP: Norris holds off Leclerc to win cagey race |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=25 May 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=5 August 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250525174653/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-monaco-gp-report/10726566/ |archive-date=25 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> and again for an incident with [[Liam Lawson]] at the latter.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/f1-2025-spanish-grand-prix-results-piastri-heads-mclaren-1-2 |title=F1 2025 Spanish Grand Prix results: Piastri heads McLaren 1–2 |date=2 June 2025 |website=[[Silverstone Circuit]] |publisher=[[British Racing Drivers' Club]] |access-date=5 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250805123630/https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/f1-2025-spanish-grand-prix-results-piastri-heads-mclaren-1-2 |archive-date=5 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Bearman claimed eleventh in the following four Grands Prix—[[2025 Canadian Grand Prix|Canada]], [[2025 Austrian Grand Prix|Austria]], [[2025 British Grand Prix|Britain]], and [[2025 Belgian Grand Prix|Belgium]];<ref name="BEL25">{{Cite web |url=https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/f1-2025-belgian-grand-prix-results-piastri-triumphs-spa |title=F1 2025 Belgian Grand Prix results: Piastri triumphs at Spa |date=28 July 2025 |website=[[Silverstone Circuit]] |publisher=[[British Racing Drivers' Club]] |access-date=5 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250805123806/https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/f1-2025-belgian-grand-prix-results-piastri-triumphs-spa |archive-date=5 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> at his first British Grand Prix, he received a ten-place grid penalty for crashing in the pit lane under red flag conditions,<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/ollie-bearman-penalty-crash-f1-british-gp-silverstone-b2783218.html |title=Ollie Bearman handed severe penalty for British GP after crash in pit-lane |last=Jackson |first=Kieran |date=5 July 2025 |work=[[The Independent]] |access-date=6 July 2025 |issn=1741-9743 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250706015835/https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/ollie-bearman-penalty-crash-f1-british-gp-silverstone-b2783218.html |archive-date=6 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> and claimed points with seventh in the Belgium sprint.<ref name="BEL25"/> He retired from the {{F1GP|2025|Hungarian}} with spontaneous [[Ground effect (cars)|floor]] damage.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.thetimes.com/sport/formula-one/article/hungarian-grand-prix-2025-race-report-standings-rkf30ljtk |url-access=subscription |title=Lando Norris leads McLaren one–two at Hungarian Grand Prix |last=Hudson |first=Molly |date=3 August 2025 |work=[[The Times]] |publisher=[[News UK]] |access-date=5 August 2025 |issn=0140-0460 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250805122915/https://www.thetimes.com/sport/formula-one/article/hungarian-grand-prix-2025-race-report-standings-rkf30ljtk |archive-date=5 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> After driving from the pit lane to sixth at the {{F1GP|2025|Dutch}},<ref>{{Cite web |last=Collantine |first=Keith |date=31 August 2025 |title=Live: 2025 Dutch Grand Prix |url=https://www.racefans.net/2025/08/31/live-2025-dutch-grand-prix/ |access-date=31 August 2025 |website=RaceFans |language=en-GB}}</ref> Bearman hit [[Carlos Sainz Jr.]] at the {{F1GP|2025|Italian}} and received a ten-second penalty and two further penalty points; classified twelfth, having incurred ten penalty points, he would be two points away from being awarded a race ban.{{efn|A driver needs to have reached the twelve penalty point threshold to be banned. The last driver to have done so is [[Kevin Magnussen]]. Bearman previously substituted for Magnussen at the [[2024 Azerbaijan Grand Prix]].}}<ref>{{Cite web |last=Collantine |first=Keith |date=7 September 2025 |title=Bearman now two penalty points away from race ban after Sainz collision |url=https://www.racefans.net/2025/09/07/bearman-now-two-penalty-points-away-from-race-ban-after-sainz-collision/ |access-date=7 September 2025 |website=RaceFans.net |language=en-GB}}</ref> After finishing twelfth again at the [[2025 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|Azerbaijan Grand Prix]],<ref>{{Cite web |title=Ocon admits 'really aggressive strategy' did not pay off |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/ocon-admits-really-aggressive-strategy-did-not-pay-off-in-baku-as-bearman.6bITwMCv1EyvQymEHTl7U |access-date=26 October 2025 |website=www.formula1.com |language=en}}</ref> Bearman scored back-to-back ninth places in [[2025 Singapore Grand Prix|Singapore]] and the [[2025 United States Grand Prix|United States]]. He was running seventh in the United States Grand Prix before a collision with [[Yuki Tsunoda]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=7 October 2025 |title=Bearman pleased with 'super important' points for Haas |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/bearman-really-happy-after-bagging-super-important-points-for-haas-in.4dD4ko3JPCl3mtj5Gr3gRG |access-date=26 October 2025 |website=www.formula1.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=20 October 2025 |title=Bearman and Tsunoda at odds over US GP clash |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/i-felt-what-he-did-was-very-dangerous-bearman-and-tsunoda-at-odds-over-us-gp.6FkUnBtP2mCrMjAsEDsf91 |access-date=26 October 2025 |website=www.formula1.com |language=en}}</ref> He finished fourth at the {{F1GP|2025|Mexico City}}—the joint-highest finish by a Haas driver since their debut in {{F1|2016}}—after climbing from ninth in the opening laps and holding off front-runners [[Kimi Antonelli]], [[George Russell (racing driver)|George Russell]], and [[Oscar Piastri]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/lucky-or-good-inside-bearmans-stellar-run-to-fourth-at-f1-mexico-gp/10772620 |title=Lucky or good? Inside Bearman's stellar run to fourth at F1 Mexico GP |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=30 October 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=30 October 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251030113620/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/lucky-or-good-inside-bearmans-stellar-run-to-fourth-at-f1-mexico-gp/10772620/ |archive-date=30 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> After a collision with Liam Lawson in the [[2025 São Paulo Grand Prix|São Paulo]] sprint,<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 November 2025 |title=2025 Sao Paulo GP Sprint: Bearman spins after contact with Lawson on Lap 1 |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/video/2025-sao-paulo-gp-sprint-bearman-spins-after-contact-with-lawson-on-lap-1.1848242551320112169 |access-date=9 November 2025 |website=Formula 1 |language=en}}</ref> Bearman secured a fourth consecutive Q3 entry and finished sixth in the race.<ref>{{Cite web |date=9 November 2025 |title=FACTS AND STATS: Verstappen P16 after first Q1 exit in years |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/facts-and-stats-verstappen-exits-in-q1-for-first-time-in-four-years-but.4rTfMBLvrxnOUv8isH21jF |access-date=9 November 2025 |website=Formula 1 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=9 November 2025 |title=FORMULA 1 MSC CRUISES GRANDE PRÊMIO DE SÃO PAULO 2025 - RACE RESULT |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results/2025/races/1273/brazil/race-result |access-date=9 November 2025 |website=Formula 1 |language=en}}</ref> His points finish in Brazil was his fourth consecutive points-scoring result, setting a new record for any Haas driver.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Khan |first=Arman |date=14 November 2025 |title=Haas Makes Historic Oliver Bearman Announcement Ahead of Vegas GP |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/article/haas-makes-historic-oliver-bearman-105900737.html |access-date=15 November 2025 |website=Yahoo Sports |language=en-US}}</ref> Bearman extended his record by finishing tenth at [[2025 Las Vegas Grand Prix|Las Vegas]], following the disqualification of both [[McLaren]] drivers.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Both McLarens disqualified from Las Vegas GP {{!}} RACER |url=https://racer.com/2025/11/23/both-mclarens-disqualified-from-las-vegas-gp |access-date=2025-11-24 |website=racer.com |language=en |archive-date=24 November 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251124012313/https://racer.com/2025/11/23/both-mclarens-disqualified-from-las-vegas-gp |url-status=dead }}</ref> In [[2025 Qatar Grand Prix|Qatar]], Bearman qualified thirteenth and retired from the race after a penalty from an unsafe release and subsequent retirement to "save the engine".<ref>{{Cite web |title=Qatar Grand Prix: Race Recap {{!}} Haas F1 Team |url=https://www.haasf1team.com/news/qatar-grand-prix-race-recap-2 |access-date=9 December 2025 |website=www.haasf1team.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Marino |first=Alex |date=3 December 2025 |title=Ollie Bearman's ‘save that engine’ quip becomes a fan favorite after painful Qatar setback - VIDEO |url=https://scuderiafans.com/ollie-bearmans-save-that-engine-quip-becomes-a-fan-favorite-after-painful-qatar-setback-video/ |access-date=9 December 2025 |website=Scuderia Fans |language=en-US}}</ref> During the final round in [[2025 Abu Dhabi Grand Prix|Abu Dhabi]], Bearman initially finished tenth, in the points, however was handed a five-second time penalty for changing direction more than once in a battle with [[Lance Stroll]] as Haas finished eighth in the Constructors' Championship.<ref>{{Cite web |date=7 December 2025 |title=FORMULA 1 ETIHAD AIRWAYS ABU DHABI GRAND PRIX 2025 - RACE RESULT |url=https://www.formula1.com/ |access-date=9 December 2025 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref>

==== 2026 ====
[[File:2026 Chinese GP - Haas - Oliver Bearman - Qualifying.jpg|alt=Bearman driving the Haas VF-26 at the 2026 Chinese Grand Prix|thumb|Bearman driving the [[Haas VF-26|VF-26]] at the [[2026 Chinese Grand Prix|Chinese Grand Prix]]]]
Bearman remained at Haas for the [[2026 Formula One World Championship|2026 season]] alongside [[Esteban Ocon]]. He began the 2026 campaign strongly at the [[2026 Australian Grand Prix|Australian Grand Prix]], finishing seventh to secure six points.<ref>{{Cite web |date=12 March 2026 |title=‘We’ve got to keep it up now’ – Bearman says points in Australia were what Haas ‘needed as a boost’ to start 2026 |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/weve-got-to-keep-it-up-now-bearman-says-points-in-australia-were-what-haas.294NHj2N9dsXeyeu7QvuKV |access-date=23 March 2026 |website=Formula One |language=en}}</ref> At the [[2026 Chinese Grand Prix|Chinese Grand Prix]], he qualified ninth for the sprint race and finished eighth to score a single point. In the main Grand Prix, despite a "deer in the headlights" moment on the opening lap where he narrowly avoided a spinning [[Isack Hadjar]], Bearman recovered to finish in fifth place.<ref>{{Cite web |date=15 March 2026 |title=Bearman overjoyed by P5 finish in China after ‘deer in the headlights’ scare with Hadjar |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/bearman-overjoyed-by-p5-finish-in-china-after-deer-in-the-headlights-scare.2Q5gywHm3hxtqzxWYJoskJ |access-date=23 March 2026 |website=Formula One |language=en}}</ref> He did not finish at the [[2026 Japanese Grand Prix|Japanese Grand Prix]] as he crashed on the twenty-second lap of the race.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-03-29 |title=Ollie Bearman’s 191mph crash is a tipping point – F1 must tweak 2026 regulations |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/ollie-bearman-crash-update-f1-2026-regulations-japanese-gp-b2947846.html |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=The Independent |language=en}}</ref> Following an eleventh place finish in [[2026 Miami Grand Prix|Miami]], he scored a point again with a tenth place finish at the [[2026 Canadian Grand Prix|Canadian Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Miami 2026 - Result • STATS F1 |url=https://www.statsf1.com/en/2026/miami/classement.aspx |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=www.statsf1.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Canada 2026 - Result • STATS F1 |url=https://www.statsf1.com/en/2026/canada/classement.aspx |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=www.statsf1.com}}</ref> This was followed by a retirement on the thirtieth lap of the [[2026 Monaco Grand Prix|Monaco Grand Prix]] due to damage to his car, and a power-related retirement on the sixty-third lap of the [[2026 Barcelona-Catalunya Grand Prix|Barcelona-Catalunya Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rogerson |first=Fleur |date=2026-06-08 |title=Ollie Bearman rues &#8216;what could have been&#8217; after F1 Monaco DNF |url=https://www.motorsportweek.com/2026/06/08/ollie-bearman-rues-what-could-have-been-after-f1-monaco-dnf/ |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=Motorsport Week |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Chokhani |first=Darshan |date=2026-06-19 |title=Bearman foresees difficult weekends for Haas after F1 Barcelona-Catalunya GP DNF |url=https://www.pitdebrief.com/post/bearman-foresees-difficult-weekends-for-haas-after-f1-barcelona-catalunya-gp-dnf/ |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=Pit Debrief |language=en-GB}}</ref> Subsequently, he finished fourteenth in [[2026 Austrian Grand Prix|Austria]], twelfth in [[2026 British Grand Prix|Silverstone]], and fourteenth again in [[2026 Belgian Grand Prix|Belgium]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Austria 2026 - Result • STATS F1 |url=https://www.statsf1.com/en/2026/autriche/classement.aspx |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=www.statsf1.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Britain 2026 - Result • STATS F1 |url=https://www.statsf1.com/en/2026/grande-bretagne/classement.aspx |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=www.statsf1.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Belgium 2026 - Result • STATS F1 |url=https://www.statsf1.com/en/2026/belgique/classement.aspx |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=www.statsf1.com}}</ref> Bearman finished nineteenth at the [[2026 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungarian Grand Prix]], having incurred a five-second time penalty for ignoring blue flags.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Hungary 2026 - Result • STATS F1 |url=https://www.statsf1.com/en/2026/hongrie/classement.aspx |access-date=2026-07-26 |website=www.statsf1.com}}</ref>

== Other racing ==
In December 2024, Bearman took part in a [[Super Formula]] test at the [[Suzuka Circuit]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Allen|first=Peter|date=9 December 2024|title=Antonelli and Bearman to take part in Super Formula test at Suzuka|url=https://formulascout.com/antonelli-and-bearman-to-take-part-in-super-formula-test-at-suzuka/126464|access-date=13 December 2024|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> He finished third in the morning session, but engine trouble hindered his progress in the afternoon session, which he described as "a bit sad".<ref>{{Cite web|last=Klein|first=Jamie|url=https://www.motorsport.com/super-formula/news/bearman-sad-that-engine-trouble-hindered-times-in-super-formula-cameo/10682126/|date=13 December 2024|title=Bearman "sad" that engine trouble hindered times in Super Formula cameo|access-date=16 December 2024|website=[[Motorsport.com]]}}</ref>

In July 2025, Bearman set a new track record at a karting track in Varberg, Sweden, which has since been reclaimed by the previous holder Elton Zevenwacht.<ref>{{Cite web |date=26 July 2025 |title=The karting record Bearman grabbed has already been reclaimed |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/the-karting-record-bearman-stole-has-already-been-reclaimed/10745273/ |access-date=28 July 2025 |website=www.autosport.com |language=en}}</ref>

